WEBVTT

1
00:05:31.999 --> 00:05:33.999
Look at our Commander! 

2
00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:38.999
Seems like he's travelled all the way from Delhi to Gazni only to eat and sleep! 

3
00:05:38.999 --> 00:05:40.999
Shareef Pasha, he has come here to get us...

4
00:05:40.999 --> 00:05:44.999
...his intentions are that we attack Delhi together.

5
00:05:44.999 --> 00:05:48.999
Oh Lord, so now the Commander wants to become the Sultan of Delhi! 

6
00:05:48.999 --> 00:05:49.999
Revolt against the Sultanate? ! 

7
00:05:49.999 --> 00:05:51.834
-This is not a rebellion...

8
00:05:51.999 --> 00:05:53.999
...it's all about our desires.

9
00:05:55.999 --> 00:05:56.999
-Yes! 

10
00:05:56.999 --> 00:05:59.999
How long will we serve the Sultanate? 

11
00:06:00.999 --> 00:06:03.999
Now I desire to be the Sultan! 

12
00:06:03.999 --> 00:06:05.999
Indeed! 

13
00:06:08.417 --> 00:06:09.999
Who is this insolent fool? 

14
00:06:23.999 --> 00:06:27.999
Marvellous! 

15
00:06:43.999 --> 00:06:47.999
Alauddin!  What have you brought? 

16
00:06:47.999 --> 00:06:51.999
Uncle, you asked me to get it! ! 

17
00:06:51.999 --> 00:06:56.999
When did I ask you to get an ostrich? 

18
00:06:57.999 --> 00:06:59.999
I do not remember.

19
00:07:00.999 --> 00:07:02.999
But Alauddin never forgets.

20
00:07:03.999 --> 00:07:07.999
I respect you so much. You asked for a feather, I got you an ostrich instead.

21
00:07:08.999 --> 00:07:11.834
Feather? Oh yes!  Now I remember...

22
00:07:11.999 --> 00:07:12.999
Now you remember! 

23
00:07:12.999 --> 00:07:13.999
For my beloved Mehru! 

24
00:07:13.999 --> 00:07:14.999
Yes, for Mehru! 

25
00:07:15.999 --> 00:07:16.999
Mehru! 

26
00:07:16.999 --> 00:07:17.999
Mehru! 

27
00:07:19.999 --> 00:07:20.999
Mehru! 

28
00:07:20.999 --> 00:07:21.999
Yes, Father? 

29
00:07:21.999 --> 00:07:24.999
Look what I got for you as a gift.

30
00:07:25.999 --> 00:07:27.999
Allah!  An Ostrich! 

31
00:07:28.999 --> 00:07:31.999
I really love you a lot, Father! 

32
00:07:31.999 --> 00:07:32.999
Me too.

33
00:07:35.999 --> 00:07:40.999
I'd like to reward you for fulfilling my daughter's wish.

34
00:07:40.999 --> 00:07:43.999
What do you want? 

35
00:07:43.999 --> 00:07:46.999
I risked my life to fulfil your wish.

36
00:07:47.999 --> 00:07:49.999
Now, I want your life in return! 

37
00:07:52.999 --> 00:07:53.999
No...no...

38
00:07:55.999 --> 00:07:58.999
I want your daughter Mehrunisa to be my wife.

39
00:08:01.999 --> 00:08:07.999
Aren't you clever?  For one precious gift you want another in return.

40
00:08:08.999 --> 00:08:13.999
Everything precious belongs only to Alauddin.

41
00:08:13.999 --> 00:08:14.999
Says who? 

42
00:08:17.999 --> 00:08:18.999
Alauddin! 

43
00:08:20.999 --> 00:08:22.999
Mehrunisa, daughter of Jalaluddin Khilji...

44
00:08:24.999 --> 00:08:26.999
...do you accept Alauddin Khilji as your husband? 

45
00:08:31.999 --> 00:08:33.999
She accepts! 

46
00:08:54.999 --> 00:08:59.999
Shareef Pasha, where is the groom? 

47
00:08:59.999 --> 00:09:01.999
Tell him that I've called him.

48
00:09:01.999 --> 00:09:03.999
I'll get him right away.

49
00:09:04.999 --> 00:09:05.999
Alauddin! 

50
00:09:07.999 --> 00:09:09.999
Alauddin! 

51
00:09:11.999 --> 00:09:15.999
What are you doing? It's your wedding night! 

52
00:09:16.999 --> 00:09:19.999
If the Commander finds out, he will have you beheaded.

53
00:09:19.999 --> 00:09:20.999
Who will tell him? 

54
00:09:21.999 --> 00:09:22.999
You? 

55
00:09:24.999 --> 00:09:27.999
You won't tell him. You are my childhood friend! 

56
00:09:28.999 --> 00:09:29.999
My confidante.

57
00:09:31.999 --> 00:09:34.999
You will never tell him.

58
00:09:35.999 --> 00:09:37.999
Never.

59
00:09:39.999 --> 00:09:40.999
Never.

60
00:09:45.999 --> 00:09:47.999
Allah! 

61
00:10:43.999 --> 00:10:50.999
Alauddin's greed to possess everything precious, made Mehru and the skies above shudder with fear.

62
00:10:51.999 --> 00:10:54.999
He believed that anything precious was rightfully his...

63
00:10:54.999 --> 00:10:59.999
... But was unaware, that thousands of miles away across the oceans...

64
00:10:59.999 --> 00:11:02.999
...lived the most precious beauty on earth...

65
00:11:02.999 --> 00:11:05.417
...the Princess of Singhal.

66
00:12:59.999 --> 00:13:02.999
Your arrow hit it's mark! ! 

67
00:13:44.999 --> 00:13:47.999
-Is anybody out there? 

68
00:13:48.999 --> 00:13:50.999
Is anybody out there? 

69
00:13:51.999 --> 00:13:52.999
Wardhan! 

70
00:13:53.999 --> 00:13:55.999
What are you doing here at this hour? 

71
00:13:56.999 --> 00:14:00.999
Our state guest, King Ratan Singh of Mewarhad set out on a hunt.

72
00:14:00.999 --> 00:14:02.999
It seems he has lost his way in the jungle.

73
00:14:02.999 --> 00:14:04.999
The King has given orders to search for him.

74
00:14:04.999 --> 00:14:08.999
Inform the King, the guest is safe and is resting in the caves.

75
00:14:08.999 --> 00:14:09.999
I shall.

76
00:14:10.999 --> 00:14:12.999
Everyone back to the Palace! 

77
00:14:18.999 --> 00:14:20.999
-Do you know what those pearls meant to me? 

78
00:14:20.999 --> 00:14:23.999
-You could've gifted him a few villages instead.

79
00:14:23.999 --> 00:14:24.999
Why did you have to give him that necklace? 

80
00:14:25.999 --> 00:14:26.834
What are you trying to say? 

81
00:14:26.999 --> 00:14:27.999
I want that necklace back.

82
00:14:28.999 --> 00:14:32.999
-It was gifted to you on our wedding and you gave it away! 

83
00:14:32.999 --> 00:14:35.999
Do not worry, i'll have a similar necklace made for you.

84
00:14:35.999 --> 00:14:37.999
Would you cross the ocean for those pearls? 

85
00:14:37.999 --> 00:14:39.999
-Those pearls were especially brought from Singhal.

86
00:14:39.999 --> 00:14:41.999
-Neither can anyone bring those pearls back...

87
00:14:41.999 --> 00:14:42.999
...nor will I ever get that necklace again.

88
00:15:10.999 --> 00:15:13.999
Have you come to apologize? 

89
00:15:16.999 --> 00:15:18.999
Your aim is remarkable.

90
00:15:18.999 --> 00:15:25.999
You wounded this hunter instead of the deer. First with your arrow and now with your eyes! 

91
00:15:26.999 --> 00:15:30.999
Our meeting was a coincidence but sometimes coincidences are beautiful...

92
00:15:30.999 --> 00:15:32.999
...just like this place of yours! 

93
00:15:32.999 --> 00:15:35.999
Everything here is so mesmerising.

94
00:15:36.999 --> 00:15:43.999
I have been talking for a while, but we know nothing about each other.

95
00:15:45.999 --> 00:15:47.999
You are Ratan Singh, the King of Mewar.

96
00:15:47.999 --> 00:15:48.999
How do you know? 

97
00:15:49.999 --> 00:15:50.999
Because you are our guest.

98
00:15:51.999 --> 00:15:54.999
And that's how you welcome your guest.

99
00:15:54.999 --> 00:15:56.999
What brings you to Singhal? 

100
00:15:57.999 --> 00:15:58.999
I'm here to buy pearls.

101
00:15:59.999 --> 00:16:02.999
Here, you don't buy pearls. You find them if you're lucky.

102
00:16:02.999 --> 00:16:03.999
Just like I found you.

103
00:16:04.999 --> 00:16:06.999
So tell me about yourself. Who are you? 

104
00:16:06.999 --> 00:16:07.999
What is your name? 

105
00:16:09.999 --> 00:16:12.999
Every leaf here knows my name.

106
00:16:13.999 --> 00:16:15.999
I'm sure you'll find out.

107
00:16:38.999 --> 00:16:40.999
She is the Princess of Singhal...

108
00:16:41.999 --> 00:16:42.999
Padmavati.

109
00:16:43.999 --> 00:16:46.834
She has been looking after you for the past two days.

110
00:16:47.999 --> 00:16:48.999
Padmavati.

111
00:16:55.999 --> 00:16:56.999
My apologies, King Ratan Singh.

112
00:16:57.999 --> 00:17:01.999
Before you could enjoy our hospitality, you got injured.

113
00:17:02.999 --> 00:17:04.999
My daughter made a grave mistake.

114
00:17:04.999 --> 00:17:06.999
It was not Padmavati's fault, king Gandharvasen.

115
00:17:06.999 --> 00:17:08.999
I glanced upon her during my hunt.

116
00:17:09.999 --> 00:17:12.999
I followed her and the arrow hit me.

117
00:17:13.417 --> 00:17:14.999
I have come to take you back.

118
00:17:14.999 --> 00:17:16.999
Please return to the Palace.

119
00:17:16.999 --> 00:17:17.999
I have stayed in palaces all my life.

120
00:17:18.999 --> 00:17:20.999
I like the tranquillity of the forest.

121
00:17:20.999 --> 00:17:23.999
If you don't mind, i'd like to stay here for a few days more.

122
00:17:25.999 --> 00:17:29.999
King Ratan Singh, you came here as our state guest...

123
00:17:29.999 --> 00:17:33.999
... But now you're more like family.

124
00:17:35.999 --> 00:17:39.999
I would like you take pearls back from Singhal and not the wound.

125
00:17:48.999 --> 00:17:50.999
-Pearls from Singhal.

126
00:17:50.999 --> 00:17:52.999
Aren't these the ones you were looking for? 

127
00:17:54.999 --> 00:17:55.999
What are you thinking? 

128
00:17:56.999 --> 00:18:00.834
Now that you've got what you wanted, you'll return to Mewar? 

129
00:18:01.999 --> 00:18:03.999
I must go back.

130
00:18:05.999 --> 00:18:06.999
You can't leave.

131
00:18:14.999 --> 00:18:16.999
Your wound hasn't healed yet.

132
00:18:18.999 --> 00:18:20.999
Would you come with me to Mewar, Padmavati? 

133
00:18:22.999 --> 00:18:23.999
As my wife! 

134
00:18:56.999 --> 00:19:01.999
With the blessings of her father, king Gandharvasen...

135
00:19:01.999 --> 00:19:05.999
Princess Padmavati got married to King Ratan Singh and left for Chittor.

136
00:19:54.999 --> 00:19:58.999
-All rise! 

137
00:19:58.999 --> 00:20:06.999
-King Ratan Singh is arriving in the court.

138
00:20:38.999 --> 00:20:42.999
All hail Queen Padmavati! 

139
00:20:42.999 --> 00:20:44.999
All hail King Ratan Singh! 

140
00:20:51.999 --> 00:20:55.999
While Chittor celebrated the arrival of it's new Queen...

141
00:20:56.999 --> 00:21:04.999
Jalaluddin revolted against the Delhi Sultanate and established the Khilji dynasty.

142
00:21:05.999 --> 00:21:08.999
He declared himself the new Sultan of Delhi.

143
00:21:08.999 --> 00:21:11.999
Sultan of Delhi, Jalaluddin Khilji...

144
00:21:11.999 --> 00:21:13.999
Glory to him! 

145
00:21:18.999 --> 00:21:23.999
But Alauddin had his eyes set on the precious throne of Delhi too.

146
00:21:23.999 --> 00:21:28.999
The throne looks beautiful from afar, but don't be deceived.

147
00:21:29.999 --> 00:21:32.999
Along with it comes it's fair share of troubles.

148
00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:40.999
We are surrounded by enemies but the most immediate threat is from the Mongols.

149
00:21:40.999 --> 00:21:44.834
Sultan, defeating the Mongols in battle is impossible.

150
00:21:44.999 --> 00:21:46.999
Our army is half their strength.

151
00:21:46.999 --> 00:21:48.999
But our courage is far greater than theirs.

152
00:21:48.999 --> 00:21:50.999
So, will you fight the Mongols? 

153
00:21:50.999 --> 00:21:53.999
For the sake of Khiljis I can even fight God.

154
00:21:53.999 --> 00:21:55.999
Well said! 

155
00:21:55.999 --> 00:22:02.834
Keep your ambitions in check, lest you get buried under their weight.

156
00:22:02.999 --> 00:22:06.999
Pardon me, but there's nothing that can come in the way of Alauddin's ambitions.

157
00:22:06.999 --> 00:22:12.999
I don't want your tall claims, only victory! 

158
00:22:12.999 --> 00:22:15.999
I will fight the Mongols.

159
00:22:16.999 --> 00:22:19.999
Sultan, your belief in me is my victory.

160
00:22:54.999 --> 00:22:56.999
Charge! 

161
00:24:05.999 --> 00:24:11.999
Alauddin defeated the Mongols and won Delhi over.

162
00:24:12.999 --> 00:24:17.999
Meanwhile, Queen Padmavati was winning hearts in Chittor.

163
00:24:21.999 --> 00:24:26.999
Careful Suraj Baisa. Your days of doing Ghoomar are long gone.

164
00:24:26.999 --> 00:24:28.999
You might hurt your back.

165
00:24:30.999 --> 00:24:33.999
Now the new Queen will perform Ghoomar. 

166
00:24:33.999 --> 00:24:37.999
My Queen, you must put up a grand performance.

167
00:24:37.999 --> 00:24:41.834
It sure will Suraj Baisa, because I will play the drums.

168
00:24:41.999 --> 00:24:42.999
Greetings, My Queen.

169
00:24:42.999 --> 00:24:46.999
Kunwar Baisa, your talkative son has spoken out of turn again.

170
00:24:47.999 --> 00:24:49.999
Leave alone playing the drums Badal...

171
00:24:50.999 --> 00:24:55.999
...no man except the King can be present during the Queen's performance.

172
00:24:55.999 --> 00:24:59.999
Son, you can beat the drums all you want at your wedding.

173
00:25:01.999 --> 00:25:03.999
-All rise for King Ratan Singh.

174
00:25:06.999 --> 00:25:09.999
Are they troubling you, My Queen? 

175
00:25:16.999 --> 00:25:20.999
The Royal Guru is expecting you at the temple.

176
00:25:25.999 --> 00:25:26.999
Shall we? 

177
00:25:35.999 --> 00:25:36.999
Welcome, My Lord! 

178
00:25:37.999 --> 00:25:42.999
Padmavati, meet the Royal Guru and my mentor, Raghav Chetan.

179
00:25:42.999 --> 00:25:44.999
He's the answer to all our questions.

180
00:25:45.999 --> 00:25:48.999
Please take his blessings.

181
00:25:57.999 --> 00:25:59.999
Your beauty is divine! 

182
00:25:59.999 --> 00:26:03.999
Not just beauty, but she's also blessed with great intelligence.

183
00:26:03.999 --> 00:26:04.999
Hmm...

184
00:26:05.999 --> 00:26:10.999
So what is more important to the new Queen? Beauty or skill? 

185
00:26:10.999 --> 00:26:13.999
Careful My Queen, you're being tested! 

186
00:26:14.999 --> 00:26:17.999
Please answer his question.

187
00:26:19.999 --> 00:26:20.999
Skill.

188
00:26:21.999 --> 00:26:22.999
And beauty? 

189
00:26:22.999 --> 00:26:24.999
That lies in the eye of the beholder.

190
00:26:24.999 --> 00:26:25.999
Please explain.

191
00:26:26.999 --> 00:26:29.999
Some see God in every object, while some see God as another object.

192
00:26:29.999 --> 00:26:30.999
-Hmm...

193
00:26:31.999 --> 00:26:33.999
Describe life in three words.

194
00:26:34.999 --> 00:26:37.999
Spirituality, love and sacrifice.

195
00:26:37.999 --> 00:26:38.999
What is love? 

196
00:26:40.999 --> 00:26:43.999
A tear of joy falling from God's eye.

197
00:26:43.999 --> 00:26:45.999
What are tears? 

198
00:26:45.999 --> 00:26:47.999
The thin line between sorrow and happiness.

199
00:26:48.417 --> 00:26:49.999
What is happiness? 

200
00:26:50.999 --> 00:26:52.999
An illusion.

201
00:26:53.999 --> 00:26:57.999
I hear you're well versed in the art of warfare.

202
00:26:57.999 --> 00:26:58.999
Yes.

203
00:26:58.999 --> 00:27:01.999
What is the greatest weapon in the battlefield? -Courage.

204
00:27:01.999 --> 00:27:03.999
Which is the most difficult moment in life? 

205
00:27:03.999 --> 00:27:05.999
Awaiting results after examination.

206
00:27:05.999 --> 00:27:07.999
And the biggest gift? 

207
00:27:10.999 --> 00:27:11.999
Blessings! 

208
00:27:20.999 --> 00:27:22.999
Come, My Queen.

209
00:27:29.999 --> 00:27:35.999
To grace this occasion...

210
00:27:35.999 --> 00:27:41.999
The Queen is arriving.

211
00:27:41.999 --> 00:27:47.999
To play a round of Ghoomar... 

212
00:27:47.999 --> 00:27:53.999
We welcome you our Queen.

213
00:28:00.999 --> 00:28:03.999
Join us in a round of Ghoomar. 

214
00:28:03.999 --> 00:28:06.999
Spin around as we play the Ghoomar. 

215
00:28:06.999 --> 00:28:09.999
Your beloved is waiting for you too.

216
00:28:09.999 --> 00:28:12.999
You blush in a new bride's glow.

217
00:28:12.999 --> 00:28:15.999
Your heart skips a beat.

218
00:28:18.999 --> 00:28:21.999
Your anklets tinkle as you walk.

219
00:28:23.999 --> 00:28:26.999
Come, My Queen...

220
00:28:26.999 --> 00:28:30.999
...let's play a round of Ghoomar!  

221
00:28:30.999 --> 00:28:33.999
Adorning the veil of love...

222
00:28:33.999 --> 00:28:38.999
...she spins in the dance of Ghoomar. 

223
00:28:38.999 --> 00:28:41.999
Without a care in the world...

224
00:28:41.999 --> 00:28:44.999
...she spins in the dance of Ghoomar. 

225
00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:46.999
Her beloved is the most special.

226
00:28:46.999 --> 00:28:53.999
She spins in the dance of Ghoomar. 

227
00:32:16.999 --> 00:32:17.999
I am lucky indeed...

228
00:32:17.999 --> 00:32:20.999
I went to Singhal looking for pearls and found you.

229
00:32:21.999 --> 00:32:23.999
I am lucky too...

230
00:32:24.999 --> 00:32:28.999
I was hunting for a deer and found a lion instead.

231
00:32:30.999 --> 00:32:33.999
I want to give you every happiness that you enjoyed in Singhal...

232
00:32:34.999 --> 00:32:35.999
... But I can't give you this one thing...

233
00:32:38.999 --> 00:32:41.999
I cannot give you the ocean in this desert.

234
00:32:41.999 --> 00:32:45.999
Your eyes are deeper than the ocean.

235
00:32:48.999 --> 00:32:52.999
Mewar seems to be growing on you.

236
00:32:52.999 --> 00:32:57.999
Mewar has found a place in my heart.

237
00:33:08.999 --> 00:33:09.417
What happened? 

238
00:33:10.417 --> 00:33:11.999
Is someone watching us? 

239
00:33:12.999 --> 00:33:17.999
Must be the moon, envious of all your extols.

240
00:33:45.999 --> 00:33:47.417
Who could it be? 

241
00:33:47.999 --> 00:33:48.999
I smell sandalwood.

242
00:33:50.999 --> 00:33:52.999
And there is only one person in Chittor who uses this fragrance.

243
00:34:20.999 --> 00:34:24.999
Why have I been summoned at this hour, My Lord? 

244
00:34:25.999 --> 00:34:27.999
An offender needs to be punished.

245
00:34:27.999 --> 00:34:29.999
Is that all? 

246
00:34:30.999 --> 00:34:33.999
This could have waited till morning.

247
00:34:33.999 --> 00:34:36.999
The crime is serious, the verdict must be given now.

248
00:34:38.999 --> 00:34:40.999
Who is the culprit? 

249
00:34:41.999 --> 00:34:42.999
You! 

250
00:34:44.999 --> 00:34:49.417
The one whose piousness Mewar  vouches for, is a culprit? 

251
00:34:49.999 --> 00:34:54.999
The one who taught you to be the King you are today, is a culprit? 

252
00:34:54.999 --> 00:34:57.999
What is my crime, My Lord? 

253
00:35:00.999 --> 00:35:05.999
You dared to pry upon the King when alone with his Queen.

254
00:35:05.999 --> 00:35:08.999
This is a lie. What proof do you have? 

255
00:35:08.999 --> 00:35:10.999
Sujaan Singh.- Yes, My Lord.

256
00:35:16.999 --> 00:35:20.999
That wound is from my dagger. And your blood is all the proof one needs.

257
00:35:21.999 --> 00:35:24.999
I thought you were my mentor, I believed in you.

258
00:35:24.999 --> 00:35:27.999
I thought you were pious, but you turned out to be a wolf in sheep's guise.

259
00:35:29.999 --> 00:35:32.999
I can sentence you to death right now...

260
00:35:33.999 --> 00:35:35.999
... But killing a Brahmin is against my principles.

261
00:35:36.999 --> 00:35:41.999
Imprison him. The darkness of the dungeon might teach him some decency.

262
00:35:41.999 --> 00:35:44.999
-Pardon me, My King. But I would like to say something.

263
00:35:45.417 --> 00:35:48.999
When one's piousness is tainted, he should be distanced from the land.

264
00:35:49.999 --> 00:35:51.999
There's only one punishment for his crime.

265
00:35:53.999 --> 00:35:55.417
Banishment.

266
00:35:55.999 --> 00:35:57.999
I agree with the Queen.

267
00:35:58.417 --> 00:36:00.999
You question my piousness? 

268
00:36:16.999 --> 00:36:19.000
There, I have swallowed this humiliation.

269
00:36:20.417 --> 00:36:23.417
But this fire raging in my heart will reduce Chittor to ashes.

270
00:36:25.999 --> 00:36:29.999
Before I leave, won't you touch my feet and take my blessings? 

271
00:36:32.999 --> 00:36:35.999
Sujaan Singh.-Yes, My Lord.

272
00:36:53.999 --> 00:36:55.999
I am going far away from this land.

273
00:36:55.999 --> 00:36:58.999
But if I don't bring Mewar down to it knees...

274
00:36:58.999 --> 00:37:02.999
...then you may assume, that Raghav Chetan never existed.

275
00:37:02.999 --> 00:37:05.999
He was a mere thought that disappeared in thin air.

276
00:37:12.999 --> 00:37:17.999
Uncle, since you gave the dominion of Kara to Uncle Alauddin, his attitude has completely changed.

277
00:37:17.999 --> 00:37:20.999
He attacked Deogiri without your permission...

278
00:37:20.999 --> 00:37:24.999
... And instead of returning to Delhi with the loot, he rode straight to Kara.

279
00:37:25.999 --> 00:37:26.999
I agree with Itaat.

280
00:37:27.999 --> 00:37:30.999
He may one day revolt against you.

281
00:37:30.999 --> 00:37:33.999
While Alauddin wields his sword for the Sultanate, My dear...

282
00:37:34.417 --> 00:37:37.999
...we sit here and make idle talk.

283
00:37:37.999 --> 00:37:40.999
But Uncle, you should be wary of him...

284
00:37:40.999 --> 00:37:44.999
Alauddin is just a tool to fill the coffers of Delhi. And that's it.

285
00:37:44.999 --> 00:37:47.999
I will set sail for Kara tomorrow.

286
00:37:47.999 --> 00:37:52.999
And bring back what is rightfully mine.

287
00:37:52.999 --> 00:37:54.999
-Glory be to God! 

288
00:37:55.999 --> 00:38:00.999
Your beauty is so enchanting, it has turned these shackles to gold.

289
00:38:02.999 --> 00:38:06.999
You will be very happy in my harem, Chitai.

290
00:38:08.999 --> 00:38:10.999
You're a slave, not a King.

291
00:38:11.999 --> 00:38:13.999
You can never make the Princess of Deogiri happy.

292
00:38:14.999 --> 00:38:15.999
Well said! 

293
00:38:16.999 --> 00:38:20.999
Such arrogance in spite of all these atrocities! 

294
00:38:21.999 --> 00:38:23.999
You have won my heart.

295
00:38:30.999 --> 00:38:31.999
Chief! -Hmm...

296
00:38:32.999 --> 00:38:33.999
Your plan has succeeded.

297
00:38:33.999 --> 00:38:35.999
Splendid! 

298
00:38:35.999 --> 00:38:38.999
You wanted the Sultan to come to Kara, and he has.

299
00:38:43.999 --> 00:38:45.999
Long live the Khiljis! 

300
00:38:45.999 --> 00:38:47.417
-Long live! 

301
00:38:47.999 --> 00:38:49.999
Alauddin welcomes the Sultan of Delhi.

302
00:38:49.999 --> 00:38:52.999
Stay blessed! 

303
00:38:52.999 --> 00:38:54.999
I am elated, as well as surprised.

304
00:38:54.999 --> 00:38:57.999
What brings you to Kara without prior notice? 

305
00:38:59.417 --> 00:39:01.999
That's exactly my question to you.

306
00:39:01.999 --> 00:39:06.999
Why have you come to  Kara instead  of returning to Delhi with the loot? 

307
00:39:06.999 --> 00:39:09.999
So the Sultan doesn't trust me anymore? 

308
00:39:09.999 --> 00:39:14.999
I've won all these treasures only for you.

309
00:39:14.999 --> 00:39:17.999
And this stone? 

310
00:39:19.999 --> 00:39:20.999
It's precious.

311
00:39:21.999 --> 00:39:23.999
A gift I gave myself.

312
00:39:31.999 --> 00:39:33.999
Glory be to God! 

313
00:39:33.999 --> 00:39:38.999
This precious gem belongs in the Sultan's crown.

314
00:39:39.999 --> 00:39:41.999
But don't be disheartened Alauddin.

315
00:39:41.999 --> 00:39:46.999
I've brought a precious gift for you too.

316
00:39:48.999 --> 00:39:49.999
This slave! 

317
00:39:54.999 --> 00:39:57.999
Especially bought for you.

318
00:39:57.999 --> 00:40:00.999
He has the guile of a wolf and the agility of a cheetah.

319
00:40:01.999 --> 00:40:06.999
He will serve you in every way possible.

320
00:40:07.999 --> 00:40:08.999
You can put him to test.

321
00:40:08.999 --> 00:40:09.999
Hmm...

322
00:40:11.999 --> 00:40:12.999
What's the name? 

323
00:40:12.999 --> 00:40:13.999
Malik Kafur, Sire.

324
00:40:14.417 --> 00:40:16.999
Not yours. The perfume you're wearing.

325
00:40:16.999 --> 00:40:18.999
Jannat-ul-Firdaus.

326
00:40:19.999 --> 00:40:21.999
What can you do for me? 

327
00:40:21.999 --> 00:40:23.999
Anything.

328
00:40:23.999 --> 00:40:26.999
I can give my life for you.

329
00:40:26.999 --> 00:40:27.999
Can you take a life for me? 

330
00:40:28.999 --> 00:40:30.999
Yes, Sire.-Hmm.

331
00:40:32.999 --> 00:40:33.999
Then kill these men.

332
00:40:34.417 --> 00:40:36.999
Kill them? 

333
00:40:37.999 --> 00:40:41.999
They are my ministers! 

334
00:40:45.999 --> 00:40:52.999
Jokes apart. I want you to march South with your army.

335
00:41:07.999 --> 00:41:08.999
Anything else, Sire? 

336
00:41:11.999 --> 00:41:13.999
What have you done? 

337
00:41:13.999 --> 00:41:14.999
You wanted me to put him to test.

338
00:41:15.999 --> 00:41:18.999
Uncle, I am really pleased with your gift.

339
00:41:19.999 --> 00:41:23.999
But don't be disheartened. I have a gift for you too.

340
00:41:23.999 --> 00:41:24.999
Ikhtiyaar! 

341
00:41:24.999 --> 00:41:26.999
My dearest Uncle! 

342
00:41:29.999 --> 00:41:32.999
Long live the Khiljis! ! 

343
00:41:36.999 --> 00:41:37.999
Long live! 

344
00:42:20.999 --> 00:42:23.999
So finally you did revolt against the Sultanate? 

345
00:42:24.999 --> 00:42:30.999
History will never forgive you for murdering my Uncle.

346
00:42:30.999 --> 00:42:34.999
What will history say Amir Khusrau? 

347
00:42:34.999 --> 00:42:37.999
History will term it the need of the hour.

348
00:42:37.999 --> 00:42:38.999
You're absolutely right.

349
00:42:39.999 --> 00:42:41.999
Itaat, my boy...

350
00:42:42.999 --> 00:42:47.999
...the Sultanate needs fresh blood to expand it’s frontiers and to keep it's people happy.

351
00:42:47.999 --> 00:42:51.999
And that is why I have seized the throne.

352
00:42:52.999 --> 00:42:58.999
And now, Jalaluddin Khilji should be buried in a manner befitting a Sultan.

353
00:43:19.999 --> 00:43:22.999
Sultan of Delhi, Alauddin Khilji...

354
00:43:22.999 --> 00:43:24.999
Long live! 

355
00:43:24.999 --> 00:43:27.999
Sultan of Delhi, Alauddin Khilji...

356
00:43:27.999 --> 00:43:30.999
Long live! 

357
00:43:42.999 --> 00:43:44.999
I am the new Sultan! 

358
00:43:48.999 --> 00:43:51.999
This is the precious stone which your father took from me...

359
00:43:51.999 --> 00:43:53.999
... And today I took away his throne.

360
00:43:54.999 --> 00:43:57.999
It's the tradition of every Sultanate.

361
00:43:58.999 --> 00:44:03.999
There's one more tradition, to bow before the Sultan.

362
00:44:05.999 --> 00:44:06.999
Hmm...

363
00:44:07.417 --> 00:44:08.999
No...no...

364
00:44:10.999 --> 00:44:11.999
Stand up.

365
00:44:19.999 --> 00:44:22.999
May the Sultan's glory prevail.

366
00:44:24.999 --> 00:44:26.999
Why do you look upset? 

367
00:44:27.999 --> 00:44:30.999
You're now the Empress of India! 

368
00:44:31.999 --> 00:44:32.999
And your husband...

369
00:44:34.999 --> 00:44:35.999
See.

370
00:44:35.999 --> 00:44:36.999
See what? 

371
00:44:37.999 --> 00:44:38.999
This crown? 

372
00:44:38.999 --> 00:44:42.999
I've seen it many a times before, on my father's head.

373
00:44:43.999 --> 00:44:45.999
This crown is unfaithful.

374
00:44:47.999 --> 00:44:48.999
Always changing heads.

375
00:44:49.999 --> 00:44:53.999
From your father's head to mine. And now on yours! 

376
00:44:59.999 --> 00:45:05.999
On this joyous occasion, make unabashed love to your Sultan.

377
00:45:07.417 --> 00:45:08.999
Now! 

378
00:45:39.999 --> 00:45:40.999
Kafur! 

379
00:45:42.999 --> 00:45:43.999
Malik Kafur! 

380
00:45:44.999 --> 00:45:45.999
Yes, Sire! 

381
00:45:51.417 --> 00:45:51.999
Yes, Sire? 

382
00:45:51.999 --> 00:45:54.999
Can you hear these strains of flute, or is it just me? 

383
00:45:54.999 --> 00:45:55.999
I do hear it.

384
00:45:56.999 --> 00:45:59.417
Who is playing the flute at this hour? 

385
00:45:59.999 --> 00:46:00.999
Should I silence him for good? 

386
00:46:00.999 --> 00:46:05.999
No. His notes are precious. Bring him to me tomorrow.

387
00:46:06.417 --> 00:46:06.999
Yes, Sire.

388
00:46:08.999 --> 00:46:10.999
Any other service? 

389
00:46:34.999 --> 00:46:36.999
Exquisite! 

390
00:46:36.999 --> 00:46:38.999
Ethereal! 

391
00:46:38.999 --> 00:46:43.999
I can conquer everything precious, except for your talent.

392
00:46:44.999 --> 00:46:47.999
What did you say your name was? Raghav Chetan.

393
00:46:49.999 --> 00:46:52.999
Whoever you are. Wherever you've come from...

394
00:46:53.999 --> 00:46:56.999
...now on you will be the pride of my court.

395
00:46:58.999 --> 00:46:59.999
What are you looking at? 

396
00:46:59.999 --> 00:47:01.999
Your past! 

397
00:47:02.999 --> 00:47:06.000
Ostrich feathers smeared with blood.

398
00:47:07.999 --> 00:47:09.999
A red stone studded crown.

399
00:47:10.999 --> 00:47:13.999
A crown that will rule the world! 

400
00:47:14.999 --> 00:47:16.999
Alexander the Great! 

401
00:47:16.999 --> 00:47:18.999
You will be the next Alexander! 

402
00:47:21.999 --> 00:47:25.999
But this is only possible when she is with you.

403
00:47:25.999 --> 00:47:26.999
Who? 

404
00:47:26.999 --> 00:47:29.999
She's an illusion! 

405
00:47:29.999 --> 00:47:32.999
A creation of God. Her face glows like moonlight.

406
00:47:35.999 --> 00:47:38.999
Her luminous beauty radiates far and beyond.

407
00:47:38.999 --> 00:47:41.999
She is the essence of life.

408
00:47:43.999 --> 00:47:45.999
A mere glimpse of her shadow would make you desire her.

409
00:47:46.999 --> 00:47:48.999
Such beauty can exist only in dreams.

410
00:47:54.999 --> 00:47:59.999
I assure you. One look at her and you’ll never be able to get her off your mind.

411
00:48:00.999 --> 00:48:03.999
She will change your destiny.

412
00:48:03.999 --> 00:48:04.999
If you win her over...

413
00:48:05.999 --> 00:48:07.999
... Mewar will be yours! 

414
00:48:07.999 --> 00:48:08.999
India will be yours! 

415
00:48:09.999 --> 00:48:11.999
The world will be at your feet, even paradise! 

416
00:48:12.999 --> 00:48:14.999
Without her, you'll have nothing.

417
00:48:15.999 --> 00:48:17.999
Whatever she touches, turns to gold! 

418
00:48:18.999 --> 00:48:21.999
She will make you immortal! 

419
00:48:21.999 --> 00:48:24.999
She is the most precious. But just as impossible to possess.

420
00:48:25.999 --> 00:48:27.999
What's the name of Alauddin's destiny? 

421
00:48:28.999 --> 00:48:31.999
The Queen of Chittor, Padmavati.

422
00:48:35.999 --> 00:48:36.999
Padmavati! 

423
00:48:37.834 --> 00:48:42.999
Greetings to King Ratan Singh of  Mewar from the Sultan of Delhi.

424
00:48:42.999 --> 00:48:46.999
I send this invitation to you on the occasion of my birthday.

425
00:48:47.999 --> 00:48:49.999
Please grace the event along with your family.

426
00:48:49.999 --> 00:48:55.999
Share a meal and enjoy our hospitality.

427
00:48:55.999 --> 00:48:57.999
So that like other kings...

428
00:48:57.999 --> 00:49:02.999
...you and Mewar stay protected under the sovereignty of Sikandar-e-Sani.

429
00:49:02.999 --> 00:49:06.999
Your well-wisher, the Sultan of Delhi, Alauddin Khilji.

430
00:49:08.999 --> 00:49:10.999
Read it once again.

431
00:49:16.999 --> 00:49:18.999
Greetings from the Sultan...

432
00:49:27.999 --> 00:49:32.999
Please inform your Sultan, we have more steel in our nerves than in his entire armoury.

433
00:49:34.999 --> 00:49:36.999
We're safe without his refuge.

434
00:49:39.999 --> 00:49:42.999
Long live the Khiljis.-Hmm.

435
00:49:42.999 --> 00:49:46.999
Sultan, The King of Chittor has declined your invitation.

436
00:49:51.999 --> 00:49:53.999
Then summon the troops and declare war.

437
00:49:53.999 --> 00:49:55.999
You should fear God, Sultan.

438
00:49:55.999 --> 00:49:57.999
Padmavati is someone's wife.

439
00:49:57.999 --> 00:50:02.999
Malik Kafur, ask the Empress what will she serve for dinner.

440
00:50:03.999 --> 00:50:05.999
Venison, Kabuli pulao, korma, aloo bukhara, shahi...

441
00:50:05.999 --> 00:50:07.999
With a feast like that I’ve no appetite left for fear.

442
00:50:08.999 --> 00:50:09.999
Hmm? 

443
00:50:13.999 --> 00:50:17.999
It's hard to believe, sikandar-e-Sani will wage war for a woman.

444
00:50:17.999 --> 00:50:20.999
I am done extending my boundaries. It's time to extend my arms.

445
00:50:21.999 --> 00:50:24.999
A war in the name of beauty! 

446
00:50:44.999 --> 00:50:45.999
What's the matter Tejveer? 

447
00:50:45.999 --> 00:50:48.999
Why have you rushed to the fort from the frontier? 

448
00:50:48.999 --> 00:50:49.999
I have a message.

449
00:50:50.999 --> 00:50:54.999
Sultan Alauddin Khilji and his army are on their way to attack Chittor.

450
00:51:58.999 --> 00:52:00.999
The Khilji army will reach Chittor soon, My Lord.

451
00:52:00.999 --> 00:52:03.999
I know. We will welcome them in true Rajput manner.

452
00:52:03.999 --> 00:52:07.999
Alert the troops and fill the granaries with supplies.

453
00:52:07.999 --> 00:52:10.999
But the people are scared.-There is nothing to fear.

454
00:52:10.999 --> 00:52:14.999
Gather all women and children from the villages and bring them inside the fort.

455
00:52:14.999 --> 00:52:17.999
Send a message to all the neighbouring Kingdoms...

456
00:52:17.999 --> 00:52:20.999
...that if we all unite, Alauddin can be defeated.

457
00:52:20.999 --> 00:52:22.999
Otherwise, he will annihilate us one by one.

458
00:52:22.999 --> 00:52:23.999
Yes, My Lord! 

459
00:52:56.999 --> 00:52:57.999
My Lord? 

460
00:53:00.999 --> 00:53:02.999
Attack! 

461
00:53:26.999 --> 00:53:29.999
Malik!  Now this war is justified.

462
00:53:29.999 --> 00:53:31.999
Absolutely, Sultan.

463
00:53:33.999 --> 00:53:36.999
Commander Ulugh Khan, what is your opinion? Should we send some of our troops? 

464
00:53:36.999 --> 00:53:36.999
Certainly, Sire.

465
00:53:37.999 --> 00:53:41.999
But Ulugh Khan, it's impossible to scale the walls of Chittor.

466
00:53:42.999 --> 00:53:44.999
Whoever tried, has only faced defeat.

467
00:53:44.999 --> 00:53:48.999
Khiljis have never accepted defeat.

468
00:53:49.417 --> 00:53:51.999
Send some troops before sunset.

469
00:53:52.999 --> 00:53:54.999
Let's gauge the ability of these Rajputs.

470
00:54:14.999 --> 00:54:17.999
I don't understand their tactic of sending a handful of soldiers, My Lord.

471
00:54:18.999 --> 00:54:20.999
With your permission, should we engage them? 

472
00:54:21.999 --> 00:54:22.999
Let them come.

473
00:55:02.999 --> 00:55:03.999
You summoned me, Sultan? 

474
00:55:04.999 --> 00:55:07.999
It's time to kill you! 

475
00:55:09.999 --> 00:55:11.999
Our decision to attack was not correct.

476
00:55:11.999 --> 00:55:13.999
I had warned Ulugh Khan...

477
00:55:13.999 --> 00:55:19.999
Let the universe be warned, the Rajput Sun will soon be eclipsed by the Khilji Crescent.

478
00:55:19.999 --> 00:55:20.999
Pardon me, Sultan.

479
00:55:21.999 --> 00:55:24.999
But passion isn't enough to break down the walls of Chittor.

480
00:55:31.999 --> 00:55:34.999
This passion is what helped me conquer half of India.

481
00:55:34.999 --> 00:55:36.999
The walls of Chittor cannot stop me.

482
00:55:36.999 --> 00:55:38.999
But the real question is...

483
00:55:38.999 --> 00:55:43.417
...if Padmavati doesn't turn out to be as precious then...

484
00:55:44.999 --> 00:55:48.999
...the number of soldiers that have died today...

485
00:55:50.999 --> 00:55:53.999
I'll cut you into the same number of pieces! 

486
00:55:55.999 --> 00:55:59.999
The Sultan is getting hungry. Bring me food.

487
00:56:08.999 --> 00:56:12.999
-Looks like Alauddin has set upall of Delhi here, My Lord! 

488
00:56:13.999 --> 00:56:17.999
This is his strategy. Show your might and shatter the enemy's morale.

489
00:56:18.999 --> 00:56:19.999
When is Diwali? 

490
00:56:20.999 --> 00:56:21.999
Next week, My Lord.

491
00:56:21.999 --> 00:56:24.999
This year's Diwali celebrations will be so grand...

492
00:56:24.999 --> 00:56:27.999
...that they will lose half the battle watching us rejoice.

493
00:56:27.999 --> 00:56:28.999
Yes, My Lord.

494
00:57:22.999 --> 00:57:24.999
Queen, why are you sitting here all alone? 

495
00:57:26.999 --> 00:57:29.999
All of Chittor is celebrating Diwali. Everyone's looking for you.

496
00:57:30.999 --> 00:57:32.999
They have lost their minds! 

497
00:57:32.999 --> 00:57:37.999
The enemy has us surrounded and we're celebrating Diwali!  

498
00:57:37.999 --> 00:57:39.999
Why do you think of them as our enemy? 

499
00:57:40.999 --> 00:57:43.999
Think of them as the new guards of Chittor.

500
00:57:45.999 --> 00:57:50.999
They can't leave, or come inside, but can only stand guard.

501
00:57:58.999 --> 00:58:00.999
Long live the Khiljis! -Hmm.

502
00:58:01.999 --> 00:58:03.999
Sultan, if you're busy we'll come back later.

503
00:58:03.999 --> 00:58:07.999
No, these are some historical records.

504
00:58:07.999 --> 00:58:10.999
I was burning the ones that don't mention my name.

505
00:58:11.999 --> 00:58:13.999
Some of these are written by you too Khusrau.

506
00:58:13.999 --> 00:58:15.999
But Sire...

507
00:58:15.999 --> 00:58:20.999
I want history to remember only me! 

508
00:58:21.999 --> 00:58:25.999
Ulugh Khan, have you cut off all supplies of food and water to Chittor? 

509
00:58:26.999 --> 00:58:26.999
Yes, Sire.

510
00:58:26.999 --> 00:58:28.999
Did you block their secret tunnels? -Yes.

511
00:58:28.999 --> 00:58:31.999
And plundered the neighbouring villages? -Yes, Sire.

512
00:58:31.999 --> 00:58:39.999
Now send a message to all the Rajput kings that helping Mewar will invite the Sultan's wrath.

513
00:58:40.999 --> 00:58:41.999
Yes, Sire.

514
00:58:41.999 --> 00:58:42.999
Dismissed.

515
00:58:42.999 --> 00:58:48.999
Sultan, it's been days since any combat. The soldiers are getting restless.

516
00:58:48.999 --> 00:58:49.999
But the war is on! 

517
00:58:50.999 --> 00:58:55.999
Between their hunger and our patience.

518
00:58:56.999 --> 00:59:01.999
But we must motivate our soldiers. Keep them entertained.

519
00:59:03.417 --> 00:59:04.999
Wrestling! 

520
00:59:05.999 --> 00:59:06.999
Announce a wrestling bout.

521
00:59:07.999 --> 00:59:09.999
I will also fight tomorrow.

522
00:59:11.999 --> 00:59:13.999
Let's wrestle! 

523
01:00:06.999 --> 01:00:10.999
Sultan! 

524
01:00:14.999 --> 01:00:18.999
Hunting games in the morning, wrestling in the evening...

525
01:00:18.999 --> 01:00:20.999
Music and debauchery at night! 

526
01:00:20.999 --> 01:00:24.999
It's a unique way to keep the army's spirits up.

527
01:00:25.999 --> 01:00:26.999
But you must consider, Sultan...

528
01:00:27.999 --> 01:00:30.999
It's been two months since we’ve been away from Delhi.

529
01:00:31.999 --> 01:00:33.999
But we're getting closer to Padmavati.

530
01:00:35.999 --> 01:00:37.834
Like the beauties of Egypt...

531
01:00:38.999 --> 01:00:45.999
...here's a celestial beauty too whose heart beats for you.

532
01:01:06.999 --> 01:01:17.999
In the land where beauty lies, beats a heart that yearns for love.

533
01:01:27.999 --> 01:01:33.999
I feel a deep burning desire within.

534
01:03:24.999 --> 01:03:26.999
What news have you brought Sujaan Singh? 

535
01:03:26.999 --> 01:03:27.999
When are the troops of other Kingdoms arriving? 

536
01:03:28.999 --> 01:03:33.999
Every Kingdom has refused to support us.

537
01:03:33.999 --> 01:03:36.999
No one wants enmity with Alauddin.

538
01:03:36.999 --> 01:03:38.999
What should we do now Gora Singh? 

539
01:03:44.999 --> 01:03:47.999
Declare war.

540
01:03:51.999 --> 01:03:55.999
My Lord, please reconsider.

541
01:03:55.999 --> 01:03:59.999
The decision is made. Chittor will fight it's own battle.

542
01:04:42.417 --> 01:04:43.999
Sultan! 

543
01:04:45.999 --> 01:04:46.999
Sultan! 

544
01:04:46.999 --> 01:04:48.999
Wake up, Sultan! 

545
01:04:49.999 --> 01:04:51.999
The Rajputs have set all our camps on fire! 

546
01:04:51.999 --> 01:04:54.999
Then put out the fire. Wake me up when it is done.

547
01:04:54.999 --> 01:04:57.999
Let's go, Sultan...-You fool, my birds! 

548
01:04:57.999 --> 01:04:59.999
They are precious! They shouldn't be harmed.

549
01:04:59.999 --> 01:05:02.999
Stop joking...

550
01:05:08.999 --> 01:05:11.999
Here are your cages! 

551
01:05:43.999 --> 01:05:45.999
Long live the Khiljis.

552
01:05:46.999 --> 01:05:49.999
The troops are growing restless, Sultan.

553
01:05:49.999 --> 01:05:54.999
Our camps, food and other reserves have burnt to ashes.

554
01:05:55.999 --> 01:05:58.999
The troops are dying of thirst.

555
01:06:00.999 --> 01:06:06.999
I have a request to make, Sire. If you could meet with the troops once.

556
01:06:08.999 --> 01:06:11.999
Your army is on the verge of mutiny.

557
01:06:27.999 --> 01:06:31.999
We won't stay here any longer.

558
01:06:31.999 --> 01:06:34.999
We will go back to Delhi! 

559
01:06:37.999 --> 01:06:40.999
Whoever wants to go back, step forward.

560
01:06:40.999 --> 01:06:43.999
Embrace your Sultan and return to Delhi.

561
01:06:46.999 --> 01:06:47.999
Ulugh Khan? 

562
01:07:17.999 --> 01:07:21.999
We Khiljis saw a dream together.

563
01:07:21.999 --> 01:07:25.999
That one day our flag will soar all over the world.

564
01:07:25.999 --> 01:07:30.999
We swore to stand by each other, come what may.

565
01:07:32.999 --> 01:07:38.999
And during these troubled times, you want to give up! 

566
01:07:41.999 --> 01:07:43.999
Then forget our dream! 

567
01:07:53.999 --> 01:07:57.999
Long live the Khiljis.-Long live! 

568
01:08:04.999 --> 01:08:08.999
 Sikandar-e-Sani... -Long live! 

569
01:08:26.999 --> 01:08:28.999
My Lord, Greetings on Holi! 

570
01:08:29.999 --> 01:08:31.999
Wish you the same.

571
01:08:31.999 --> 01:08:33.999
I am just returning from the granary.

572
01:08:33.999 --> 01:08:35.999
We only have a few days' supply left.

573
01:08:35.999 --> 01:08:37.999
But this should remain only between us.

574
01:08:38.999 --> 01:08:40.999
Our people shouldn't know.

575
01:08:40.999 --> 01:08:42.999
Our difficulties are growing, My Lord.

576
01:08:42.999 --> 01:08:45.999
Difficulties will also grow for our enemy.

577
01:08:46.999 --> 01:08:50.999
This scorching heat will force Alauddin to retreat.

578
01:08:50.999 --> 01:08:52.999
Just a few more days.

579
01:08:52.999 --> 01:08:57.999
Please enjoy Holi. I'll go and wish the new Queen on her first Holi here.

580
01:09:00.999 --> 01:09:01.999
Please don't ignore the reality, My Lord.

581
01:09:02.999 --> 01:09:03.999
This is a matter of grave concern.

582
01:09:05.999 --> 01:09:07.999
You seem to have forgotten, Gora Singh.

583
01:09:08.999 --> 01:09:12.999
One who braves any situation, is a Rajput.

584
01:09:13.999 --> 01:09:17.999
One who dares to walk on burning embers, is a Rajput.

585
01:09:18.999 --> 01:09:22.999
One who accepts all challenges and emerges victorious, is a Rajput.

586
01:09:22.999 --> 01:09:30.999
The one who fights the enemy till his last breath, is a Rajput.

587
01:09:31.999 --> 01:09:32.999
Sultan! 

588
01:09:36.999 --> 01:09:38.999
These people have lost their minds! 

589
01:09:38.999 --> 01:09:42.999
They celebrate despite the siege. I see colours flying from the fort! 

590
01:09:42.999 --> 01:09:47.999
-Colours are bound to fly in Chittor. Today is Holi!  

591
01:09:48.999 --> 01:09:50.999
People colour each other and express their love.

592
01:09:50.999 --> 01:09:53.999
And even embrace their enemies? 

593
01:09:53.999 --> 01:09:54.999
Yes, Sire.

594
01:09:54.999 --> 01:09:57.999
Then let me play with the enemy too! 

595
01:09:57.999 --> 01:09:59.999
With colours or blood? 

596
01:10:03.999 --> 01:10:09.999
Before this weather turns against us, send a message of truce to the fort.

597
01:10:10.999 --> 01:10:12.999
Truce with Chittor? 

598
01:10:12.999 --> 01:10:15.999
Why did your face turn pale? -Absolutely not! 

599
01:10:16.999 --> 01:10:17.999
I will deliver this message...

600
01:10:17.999 --> 01:10:19.999
Not you, Malik Kafur will go.

601
01:10:20.999 --> 01:10:21.999
As you wish.

602
01:10:21.999 --> 01:10:23.999
So today is Holi!  

603
01:10:23.999 --> 01:10:26.999
Someone colour me too.

604
01:11:15.999 --> 01:11:22.999
The Festival of Colours is here.

605
01:11:32.999 --> 01:11:35.999
I will play Holi with my beloved.

606
01:11:35.999 --> 01:11:39.999
And colour him with my love.

607
01:13:28.999 --> 01:13:30.999
Chief, look! 

608
01:13:33.999 --> 01:13:36.999
Should I knock him down? 

609
01:13:36.999 --> 01:13:38.999
Let him come, Badal.

610
01:13:50.999 --> 01:13:52.999
This is Malik Kafur, My Lord.

611
01:13:52.999 --> 01:13:56.999
Alauddin's most trusted. Some even call him his consort.

612
01:14:00.999 --> 01:14:03.999
Greetings to King Ratan Singh from the Sultan of Delhi.

613
01:14:04.999 --> 01:14:10.999
I've understood that the Rajputs of Mewar don't  bow their heads or swords.

614
01:14:10.999 --> 01:14:13.999
Your determination is truly commendable.

615
01:14:13.999 --> 01:14:16.999
I would like to extend my hand in friendship towards you.

616
01:14:16.999 --> 01:14:22.999
Before returning to Delhi, I would like to experience Chittor's hospitality.

617
01:14:23.999 --> 01:14:27.999
I hope you will accept my message of truce.

618
01:14:29.999 --> 01:14:31.999
I will definitely meet Alauddin.

619
01:14:31.999 --> 01:14:34.999
Marvellous! The Sultan will be very pleased! 

620
01:14:35.999 --> 01:14:37.999
But before we meet, I have certain conditions.

621
01:14:37.999 --> 01:14:39.999
We accept all your conditions.

622
01:14:39.999 --> 01:14:41.999
At least listen to the conditions.

623
01:14:51.999 --> 01:14:55.999
This proposition could be a conspiracy.

624
01:14:58.999 --> 01:14:59.999
Could be.

625
01:15:01.999 --> 01:15:04.999
Then why invite the Sultan to the fort? 

626
01:15:05.999 --> 01:15:08.999
I accepted his proposal and rejected it as well.

627
01:15:08.999 --> 01:15:10.999
How is that? -I proposed two conditions.

628
01:15:10.999 --> 01:15:12.999
First, his army must return to Delhi.

629
01:15:13.999 --> 01:15:20.999
Second, if he would like to meet me, he must come to the fort alone and unarmed.

630
01:15:20.999 --> 01:15:23.999
What if he accepts your conditions? 

631
01:15:24.999 --> 01:15:27.999
A man who came all the way from Delhi and spent six months in the scorching heat...

632
01:15:27.999 --> 01:15:29.999
...would definitely accept your conditions.

633
01:15:30.999 --> 01:15:31.999
I don't think so.

634
01:15:31.999 --> 01:15:34.999
Lord Ram too never thought that Raavan will come disguised as a sage.

635
01:15:40.999 --> 01:15:42.999
Greetings, My Lord. Pardon me for my untimely interruption.

636
01:15:43.999 --> 01:15:44.999
What is it Gora Singh? 

637
01:15:44.999 --> 01:15:46.999
The Sultan has sent a message.

638
01:15:46.999 --> 01:15:48.999
He has accepted both our conditions.

639
01:15:53.999 --> 01:15:54.999
Let him come.

640
01:16:07.999 --> 01:16:11.999
 Prayer chants... 

641
01:16:15.999 --> 01:16:17.999
Is the army ready to return to Delhi? 

642
01:16:18.999 --> 01:16:20.999
Is the Sultan really sending the army away from Chittor? 

643
01:16:20.999 --> 01:16:24.999
Away from Chittor's sight but not from their land! 

644
01:16:24.999 --> 01:16:25.999
Pardon me, Sultan.

645
01:16:26.999 --> 01:16:29.999
But entering the enemy's fort unarmed can be dangerous.

646
01:16:44.999 --> 01:16:45.999
Danger! 

647
01:16:52.999 --> 01:16:53.999
I accept! 

648
01:16:56.999 --> 01:17:00.999
Every danger that takes Alauddin closer to Padmavati.

649
01:17:03.999 --> 01:17:05.999
I accept.

650
01:17:11.999 --> 01:17:12.999
I accept.

651
01:17:27.999 --> 01:17:32.999
By the way Sultan, delhi's throne is in danger too.

652
01:17:33.999 --> 01:17:34.999
Itaat Khan! 

653
01:17:35.999 --> 01:17:40.999
His eyes are full of hatred for you and greed for the throne.

654
01:17:41.999 --> 01:17:43.999
He wants to be the next Sultan.

655
01:17:56.999 --> 01:18:02.999
Every star wants to be the moon but never succeeds.

656
01:18:03.999 --> 01:18:09.999
Like I am so close to you, but can never take Padmavati's place.

657
01:18:13.999 --> 01:18:16.999
Queen Padmavati! 

658
01:20:38.999 --> 01:20:40.999
Welcome to the fort, Sultan.

659
01:20:40.999 --> 01:20:43.999
King Ratan Singh! 

660
01:20:43.999 --> 01:20:46.999
Pardon me, but I am the Commander of Mewar's army.

661
01:20:47.999 --> 01:20:49.999
Gora Singh.

662
01:20:50.999 --> 01:20:53.999
So where is your King Ratan Singh hiding? 

663
01:20:54.999 --> 01:20:56.999
He's waiting for you inside.

664
01:21:29.999 --> 01:21:34.999
I feel elated today! 

665
01:21:35.999 --> 01:21:38.999
I feel on top of the world today! 

666
01:21:43.999 --> 01:21:43.999
Wonderful! 

667
01:21:44.999 --> 01:21:47.999
Pardon me, but I am overwhelmed to see you.

668
01:21:49.999 --> 01:21:52.999
After months of waiting, we finally meet! 

669
01:21:52.999 --> 01:21:57.999
Now that you're here, how would you like to be welcomed? 

670
01:21:58.999 --> 01:21:59.999
Like a dear friend! 

671
01:22:11.999 --> 01:22:12.999
I've got you a precious gift! 

672
01:22:13.999 --> 01:22:16.999
You're gifting a sword to a friend? 

673
01:22:16.999 --> 01:22:21.999
It was one of your conditions, wasn't it? To come alone and unarmed.

674
01:22:22.999 --> 01:22:25.999
Here. Now I am unarmed.

675
01:22:29.999 --> 01:22:31.999
I've heard it's very beautiful...

676
01:22:32.999 --> 01:22:34.999
...the Fort of Chittor! 

677
01:22:35.999 --> 01:22:38.999
God has truly blessed Rajputs with abundance.

678
01:22:38.999 --> 01:22:41.999
Abundant skills!  Such grandeur! 

679
01:22:42.999 --> 01:22:44.999
And an unmatched enemy too! 

680
01:22:47.999 --> 01:22:48.999
Shall we? 

681
01:22:57.999 --> 01:23:00.999
 Prayer before meal. 

682
01:23:46.999 --> 01:23:47.999
-Your move.

683
01:23:49.999 --> 01:23:49.999
Sultan! 

684
01:23:49.999 --> 01:23:50.999
Hmm...

685
01:23:54.999 --> 01:23:59.999
Careful King. Your Queen is in danger! 

686
01:24:07.999 --> 01:24:08.999
There...

687
01:24:10.999 --> 01:24:12.999
I saved my Queen.

688
01:24:12.999 --> 01:24:13.999
Hmm...

689
01:24:13.999 --> 01:24:14.999
What are you looking at? 

690
01:24:15.999 --> 01:24:17.999
It's almost sundown.

691
01:24:17.999 --> 01:24:20.999
I guess Chittor and Delhi will have to reconcile in this game as well! 

692
01:24:23.999 --> 01:24:25.999
Well then, allow me to take your leave.

693
01:24:25.999 --> 01:24:26.999
As you please.

694
01:24:28.999 --> 01:24:30.999
But before I leave you must introduce me to your family.

695
01:24:30.999 --> 01:24:33.999
I've introduced you to everyone. This is my family.

696
01:24:34.999 --> 01:24:35.999
Yes, of course they are.

697
01:24:35.999 --> 01:24:37.999
But I was referring to the pride of Chittor...

698
01:24:38.999 --> 01:24:40.834
Queen Padmavati.

699
01:24:43.999 --> 01:24:47.999
What's wrong? Was my request unreasonable? 

700
01:24:49.999 --> 01:24:52.999
That was a disgraceful thing to say Alauddin.

701
01:24:53.999 --> 01:24:58.999
We treat our guests like God in Chittor, otherwise you would be beheaded right away! 

702
01:25:06.999 --> 01:25:09.999
Now the King is in danger too! 

703
01:25:11.999 --> 01:25:12.999
Check.

704
01:25:23.999 --> 01:25:28.999
Reconsider your decision, My Queen.

705
01:25:28.999 --> 01:25:31.999
I will never agree to this. This is wrong.

706
01:25:31.999 --> 01:25:34.999
My decision is right for Mewar, Kunwar Baisa.

707
01:25:34.999 --> 01:25:36.999
But, the King...

708
01:25:41.999 --> 01:25:43.999
Which decision of yours is right? 

709
01:25:43.999 --> 01:25:46.999
-I am aware...-You may be the Queen of Mewar but...

710
01:25:46.999 --> 01:25:48.999
...you have no right to take political decisions.

711
01:25:48.999 --> 01:25:49.999
It is my right! 

712
01:25:50.999 --> 01:25:54.999
Especially, if I am the reason for Chittor to go to war.

713
01:25:54.999 --> 01:25:57.999
So let there be a war! We will fight them in the battlefield.

714
01:25:58.999 --> 01:26:02.999
But never make the mistake of taking these decisions yourself.

715
01:26:03.999 --> 01:26:04.999
Never, My Queen.

716
01:26:06.999 --> 01:26:08.999
You made a mistake too.

717
01:26:10.999 --> 01:26:12.999
When you drew your sword, you should've beheaded him.

718
01:26:12.999 --> 01:26:14.999
You had your opportunity to change history.

719
01:26:16.999 --> 01:26:17.999
What are you saying, My Queen? 

720
01:26:18.999 --> 01:26:22.999
You know that I could've never struck an unarmed guest in the fort.

721
01:26:23.999 --> 01:26:24.999
Even if it's the Devil himself.

722
01:26:25.999 --> 01:26:30.999
History can turn its page but Rajputs don't budge from their principles.

723
01:26:38.999 --> 01:26:40.999
Then take your sword and behead me.

724
01:26:42.999 --> 01:26:44.999
Rajput principles and honour will remain intact.

725
01:26:44.999 --> 01:26:48.999
No one will ever understand your decision of showing him your face.

726
01:26:48.999 --> 01:26:50.999
Future generations will hold you accountable.

727
01:26:50.999 --> 01:26:51.999
So let them.

728
01:26:52.999 --> 01:26:56.999
If I can save even one life by showing my face, then I accept this humiliation.

729
01:26:59.999 --> 01:27:02.999
Let me fulfil my duties as the Queen.

730
01:27:08.999 --> 01:27:10.999
Wait here. The King shall join you shortly.

731
01:27:11.999 --> 01:27:12.999
Here? 

732
01:27:15.999 --> 01:27:18.999
Lord Shiva drank poison to save the world.

733
01:27:19.999 --> 01:27:22.999
Today you're taking this difficult decision for Mewar.

734
01:27:23.999 --> 01:27:24.999
Keep this with you, My Queen.

735
01:27:25.999 --> 01:27:27.999
This holy smoke will protect you from the Sultan's evil-eye.

736
01:27:30.999 --> 01:27:32.999
King Ratan Singh! 

737
01:27:32.999 --> 01:27:35.999
A thought crossed my mind while waiting...

738
01:27:38.999 --> 01:27:40.999
Gora Singh...

739
01:27:41.999 --> 01:27:43.999
Yes, My Lord.

740
01:28:10.999 --> 01:28:12.999
You may leave, Alauddin.

741
01:28:16.999 --> 01:28:19.999
Yes, I can.

742
01:28:21.999 --> 01:28:28.999
But before I return to Delhi, allow me to show you my hospitality as well.

743
01:28:30.999 --> 01:28:31.999
Tomorrow.

744
01:28:32.999 --> 01:28:33.999
I'll be waiting.

745
01:28:55.999 --> 01:28:57.999
Keep your sword with you.

746
01:28:58.999 --> 01:29:00.999
I've been invited for a meal, not for battle.

747
01:29:01.999 --> 01:29:05.999
A storm is expected outside. Think about this again.

748
01:29:06.999 --> 01:29:07.999
Do you have to go? 

749
01:29:07.999 --> 01:29:12.999
Would you like history to remember that Alauddin Khilji came to Chittor unarmed...

750
01:29:12.999 --> 01:29:15.999
... But King Ratan Singh was too scared to venture out.

751
01:29:16.999 --> 01:29:18.999
I understand your concern.

752
01:29:18.999 --> 01:29:20.999
But he is all alone. His army has gone back.

753
01:29:22.999 --> 01:29:23.999
But it can come back too.

754
01:29:29.999 --> 01:29:31.999
I shall be back before the moon rises.

755
01:29:32.999 --> 01:29:33.999
Hmm.

756
01:30:17.999 --> 01:30:18.999
Sultan! 

757
01:30:19.999 --> 01:30:20.999
Oh...

758
01:30:22.999 --> 01:30:25.999
Welcome, my friend! 

759
01:30:25.999 --> 01:30:27.999
I thought you might not show up in this storm.

760
01:30:27.999 --> 01:30:30.999
Storms like these can never stop me.

761
01:30:30.999 --> 01:30:31.999
Of course! 

762
01:30:33.999 --> 01:30:34.999
Take a seat.

763
01:30:36.999 --> 01:30:36.999
Here? 

764
01:30:36.999 --> 01:30:37.999
Yes.

765
01:30:40.999 --> 01:30:44.999
Today is my last day in Chittor. I am overwhelmed.

766
01:30:44.999 --> 01:30:45.999
Hmm...

767
01:30:46.999 --> 01:30:48.999
I have so many memories of this place.

768
01:30:48.999 --> 01:30:54.999
Many of my soldiers died here, right before my eyes.

769
01:30:56.999 --> 01:30:57.999
Do you remember? 

770
01:30:58.999 --> 01:31:00.999
The day you stood watching from the fort.

771
01:31:02.999 --> 01:31:04.999
Poor men! 

772
01:31:05.999 --> 01:31:06.999
Poor Dilnawaz! ! 

773
01:31:07.999 --> 01:31:09.999
My precious little bird! 

774
01:31:11.999 --> 01:31:17.999
The day you burnt our tents, he too perished in that fire.

775
01:31:19.999 --> 01:31:25.999
Had he been alive, you would have heard his screams in this storm.

776
01:31:31.999 --> 01:31:33.999
Anyway...

777
01:31:35.999 --> 01:31:39.999
I feel a strange connection to this soil.

778
01:31:40.999 --> 01:31:42.999
I want to take it back with me...

779
01:31:45.999 --> 01:31:46.999
... And you too! 

780
01:31:59.999 --> 01:32:02.999
So this is the Khilji hospitality? 

781
01:32:03.999 --> 01:32:04.999
Your principles? 

782
01:32:06.999 --> 01:32:09.999
I made a mistake of trusting you again Alauddin.

783
01:32:10.999 --> 01:32:14.999
Even God doesn't trust Alauddin! 

784
01:32:17.999 --> 01:32:18.999
You broke my trust too! 

785
01:32:19.999 --> 01:32:22.999
You dropped the curtains so quick that I couldn't even see the Queen's face.

786
01:32:23.999 --> 01:32:25.999
Now please don't refuse to come with me.

787
01:32:26.999 --> 01:32:29.999
Because you're the bait that will draw Queen Padmavati to Delhi.

788
01:32:29.999 --> 01:32:33.999
And if that doesn't happen, I will take Chittor away from you.

789
01:32:34.999 --> 01:32:36.999
You will take away Chittor? 

790
01:32:36.999 --> 01:32:40.999
You can take me away from Chittor, but not my pride.

791
01:32:40.999 --> 01:32:43.999
You can steal a diamond, but not it's sparkle.

792
01:32:44.999 --> 01:32:46.999
Imprison him.

793
01:32:50.999 --> 01:32:57.999
You may imprison me, but can you contain the storm rising from Chittor? 

794
01:32:58.999 --> 01:33:01.999
-Long live the Khiljis! 

795
01:33:01.999 --> 01:33:03.999
Long live! 

796
01:33:12.999 --> 01:33:14.999
Greetings, My Lord! 

797
01:33:34.999 --> 01:33:36.999
My Queen, please return to the Palace.

798
01:33:37.999 --> 01:33:39.834
A storm is gathering outside.

799
01:33:39.999 --> 01:33:43.999
And do not worry. God's blessings are with the King.

800
01:33:43.999 --> 01:33:45.999
He will return safe and sound.

801
01:33:45.999 --> 01:33:46.999
No, Kunwar Baisa.

802
01:33:48.999 --> 01:33:49.999
I will wait here until the moon rises.

803
01:33:50.999 --> 01:33:53.999
But the moon won't rise, My Queen. Tonight is a new moon! 

804
01:34:28.999 --> 01:34:30.999
My Lord! 

805
01:34:30.999 --> 01:34:33.999
Gora Singh, are you looking for your King? 

806
01:34:34.999 --> 01:34:36.999
The storm blew him away to Delhi.

807
01:34:37.999 --> 01:34:39.999
He's been banished from his own kingdom! 

808
01:34:41.999 --> 01:34:46.999
So you're the one who brought Alauddin to Chittor! 

809
01:34:49.999 --> 01:34:49.999
Traitor! 

810
01:34:50.999 --> 01:34:53.999
If you even lay a finger on me, your King will lose his life.

811
01:34:53.999 --> 01:34:55.999
There's a message for Queen Padmavati.

812
01:34:56.999 --> 01:35:02.999
If she wishes to see her King alive, she must come there! 

813
01:35:17.999 --> 01:35:30.999
O Motherland!  Give us the strength; to defend the pride of Rajputs.

814
01:35:31.999 --> 01:35:42.999
The hills of Mewar; uphold our honour now.

815
01:35:57.999 --> 01:36:01.999
Hurry!  The Queen has called us.

816
01:36:07.999 --> 01:36:10.999
Queen Nagmati has asked all the women...

817
01:36:10.999 --> 01:36:11.999
What's this? 

818
01:36:12.999 --> 01:36:14.999
Why are you smearing mud on the mirrors? 

819
01:36:15.999 --> 01:36:18.999
Until the King returns, I won't see my face in the mirror.

820
01:36:18.999 --> 01:36:20.999
But, My Queen...-What is it? 

821
01:36:22.999 --> 01:36:24.999
Queen Nagmati has called all the women.

822
01:36:25.999 --> 01:36:26.999
And you too.

823
01:36:47.999 --> 01:36:49.999
Why have you called us? 

824
01:36:49.999 --> 01:36:50.999
Go away! 

825
01:36:50.999 --> 01:36:52.999
Queen, did you call me? 

826
01:36:52.999 --> 01:36:54.999
At least let me grieve in peace! 

827
01:36:56.000 --> 01:37:00.999
If you hadn't banished the Royal Guru, he wouldn't have joined hands with Alauddin.

828
01:37:00.999 --> 01:37:02.999
And Chittor would not be under threat! 

829
01:37:03.999 --> 01:37:07.999
Today our King is in the enemy's clutches and it's entirely your fault! 

830
01:37:08.999 --> 01:37:09.999
Your beauty is to be blamed! 

831
01:37:10.999 --> 01:37:12.999
What about the beholder? 

832
01:37:14.999 --> 01:37:15.999
And his sinful gaze? 

833
01:37:15.999 --> 01:37:19.999
They too are at fault. And Mewar is paying the price for that.

834
01:37:19.999 --> 01:37:21.999
But you should face punishment too! 

835
01:37:21.999 --> 01:37:25.999
How to punish someone who is not at fault? 

836
01:37:26.999 --> 01:37:29.999
Poison her?  Throw her in the well? Or imprison her? 

837
01:37:29.999 --> 01:37:34.999
We should accept the Sultan's condition and send Padmavati there.

838
01:37:36.999 --> 01:37:40.999
My Queen!  How can you say that being a woman yourself? 

839
01:37:41.417 --> 01:37:42.999
Send her there? 

840
01:37:43.417 --> 01:37:45.999
Hand her over to the Sultan? Impossible! 

841
01:37:47.999 --> 01:37:51.999
If we don't comply, neither our King nor Mewar will survive! 

842
01:37:51.999 --> 01:37:52.999
-My Queen! 

843
01:37:54.999 --> 01:37:57.999
If the time comes for such desperate measures...

844
01:37:57.999 --> 01:38:03.999
...then every woman in Chittor will jump into the fire to protect her dignity.

845
01:38:04.999 --> 01:38:06.999
We'll perform Jauhar! 

846
01:38:07.999 --> 01:38:12.999
But we will never let our Queen set foot out of this fort.

847
01:38:14.999 --> 01:38:17.999
How do I explain my grief to you all? 

848
01:38:22.999 --> 01:38:23.999
I shall go.

849
01:38:25.999 --> 01:38:27.999
What are you saying, My Queen? 

850
01:38:28.417 --> 01:38:31.999
Even the Goddess had to descend from her abode to slay the demons.

851
01:38:33.999 --> 01:38:37.999
Who am I?  A mere mortal. I will only cross the threshold of Chittor.

852
01:38:39.999 --> 01:38:41.999
And you forget, My Queen.

853
01:38:42.999 --> 01:38:46.999
Rajput women are just as much warriors as their men.

854
01:39:17.999 --> 01:39:18.999
-My Lord! 

855
01:39:19.999 --> 01:39:23.999
I had told you! I will bring Mewar down to its knees.

856
01:39:23.999 --> 01:39:27.999
I can feel your pain. That's why I play the flute.

857
01:39:27.999 --> 01:39:29.999
 Raag Yaman!  

858
01:39:29.999 --> 01:39:32.999
Did it alleviate some of your sorrows? 

859
01:39:32.999 --> 01:39:34.999
It can't.

860
01:39:35.999 --> 01:39:38.999
Your music once felt like sandalwood.

861
01:39:39.999 --> 01:39:39.999
And now? 

862
01:39:39.999 --> 01:39:41.999
It stinks! 

863
01:39:42.999 --> 01:39:43.999
Stinks of treason.

864
01:39:44.999 --> 01:39:47.999
You've lost your crown, but not your pride.

865
01:39:47.999 --> 01:39:52.999
Not until I have the enemy's head at my feet.

866
01:39:52.999 --> 01:39:54.999
That's impossible! 

867
01:39:54.999 --> 01:40:01.417
Raghav Chetan's fury has turned your stars unfavourable for you.

868
01:40:02.999 --> 01:40:05.999
You will have to bow before the Sultan.

869
01:40:07.999 --> 01:40:10.999
Play on! Yaman. 

870
01:40:29.999 --> 01:40:30.999
Greetings, My Queen.

871
01:40:32.999 --> 01:40:35.999
This sword had sworn to protect Mewari pride.

872
01:40:35.999 --> 01:40:38.999
But you've decided to go there.

873
01:40:38.999 --> 01:40:39.999
You have embarrassed us.

874
01:40:40.999 --> 01:40:42.999
Take this sword and behead me.

875
01:40:43.999 --> 01:40:45.999
This is the only way to bring our King back.

876
01:40:45.999 --> 01:40:51.999
Don't you trust our ability to bring our King back? 

877
01:40:51.999 --> 01:40:52.999
I do! 

878
01:40:52.999 --> 01:40:57.999
But not every war is won with might. This time we'll have to use a different strategy.

879
01:40:57.999 --> 01:40:59.999
Our swords...-Send a message to the Sultan.

880
01:40:59.999 --> 01:41:02.999
I don't agree with your decision.

881
01:41:02.999 --> 01:41:04.999
As your brother...

882
01:41:05.999 --> 01:41:09.999
This is not a request from a sister, but an order of the Queen of Mewar! 

883
01:41:15.999 --> 01:41:19.999
For the sake of King of Mewar's safety, queen Padmavati has agreed to come here.

884
01:41:20.999 --> 01:41:22.999
Congratulations Sultan! Your wish has come true.

885
01:41:22.999 --> 01:41:24.999
Keep reading...-Yes.

886
01:41:24.999 --> 01:41:26.999
But she has few conditions.

887
01:41:26.999 --> 01:41:29.999
The Queen will bring eight hundred maids along.

888
01:41:29.999 --> 01:41:30.999
Agreed.

889
01:41:31.999 --> 01:41:35.999
They will stay at the women's chamber, where no men can go.

890
01:41:35.999 --> 01:41:36.999
Agreed.

891
01:41:37.999 --> 01:41:42.999
Upon her arrival, she will meet the King first. And meet the Sultan only after the King is released.

892
01:41:43.999 --> 01:41:44.999
Agreed.

893
01:41:45.417 --> 01:41:46.999
And her last condition...

894
01:41:48.999 --> 01:41:51.999
This is not possible, Sultan.

895
01:41:51.999 --> 01:41:53.999
What does she want? 

896
01:41:53.999 --> 01:42:00.999
That palanquins won't leave Chittor until Raghav Chetan's severed head is delivered to her.

897
01:42:02.999 --> 01:42:04.999
Agreed! 

898
01:42:06.999 --> 01:42:07.999
This is unfair, Sultan.

899
01:42:08.999 --> 01:42:10.999
Don't forget that Queen Padmavati will soon be yours only because of me...

900
01:42:10.999 --> 01:42:12.999
Agreed! 

901
01:42:23.999 --> 01:42:25.999
Greetings, My Queen.

902
01:42:26.999 --> 01:42:27.999
What happened, Gora Singh? 

903
01:42:27.999 --> 01:42:29.999
Khiljis have sent a reply to your message.

904
01:42:30.999 --> 01:42:32.999
Alauddin has accepted all your conditions.

905
01:42:33.999 --> 01:42:35.999
And has also sent a gift for you.

906
01:42:44.999 --> 01:42:47.999
Forgive me, My Queen. We doubted your acumen.

907
01:42:48.999 --> 01:42:51.999
You eliminated our enemy sitting here in Chittor.

908
01:42:51.999 --> 01:42:54.417
And now it's the Sultan's turn.

909
01:42:56.999 --> 01:42:58.999
But it's an impossible task without your support.

910
01:42:58.999 --> 01:43:06.999
We swear on the Almighty. Every Rajput sword will now obey your command.

911
01:43:07.999 --> 01:43:10.999
Then take out the palanquins. We will leave tomorrow.

912
01:43:10.999 --> 01:43:12.999
As you say, My Queen.

913
01:43:12.999 --> 01:43:16.999
I haven't seen the King's face in a long time.

914
01:44:08.999 --> 01:44:12.999
My heart is aloof from the world! 

915
01:44:12.999 --> 01:44:15.999
My heart is aloof from the world! 

916
01:44:15.999 --> 01:44:17.834
Well said! 

917
01:44:17.999 --> 01:44:20.999
Ever since I'm consumed by love! 

918
01:44:20.999 --> 01:44:21.999
Well said!  Very nice! 

919
01:44:21.999 --> 01:44:23.999
Now pay attention, Khusrau.

920
01:44:23.999 --> 01:44:26.999
All my heart strings are tugged.

921
01:44:27.999 --> 01:44:30.999
I've lost all slumber and peace.

922
01:44:31.999 --> 01:44:34.999
My eyes are clouded with dreams! 

923
01:44:35.999 --> 01:44:38.999
Well said!  Marvellous! 

924
01:44:39.999 --> 01:44:41.999
Did you notice? 

925
01:44:41.999 --> 01:44:46.999
Our most renowned poet, amir Khusrau praised my poetry.

926
01:44:46.999 --> 01:44:48.999
But it seems Itaat Khan didn't quite like it.

927
01:44:49.999 --> 01:44:53.417
Sultan, I don't understand such poetry.

928
01:44:53.999 --> 01:44:55.999
Because you don't understand love! 

929
01:44:55.999 --> 01:44:57.999
You're not a poet, you're a coward! 

930
01:45:01.999 --> 01:45:05.999
There's no reason to feel offended by the Sultan's words.

931
01:45:05.999 --> 01:45:09.999
That was no joke, it was an insult Ashfaq. I cannot tolerate this anymore.

932
01:45:09.999 --> 01:45:10.999
Now either the Sultan will live or me.

933
01:45:10.999 --> 01:45:11.999
What do you want to say? 

934
01:45:12.999 --> 01:45:17.999
The court will celebrate tonight. It's the right time to seize the throne! 

935
01:45:52.999 --> 01:45:55.999
My heart is soaring in the skies! 

936
01:45:59.999 --> 01:46:03.999
My heart is soaring in the skies! 

937
01:46:06.999 --> 01:46:10.999
My beloved! 

938
01:46:17.999 --> 01:46:20.999
Ever since I'm consumed by love! 

939
01:46:20.999 --> 01:46:27.999
My heart is aloof from the world! 

940
01:48:48.999 --> 01:48:51.999
May Allah accept our prayers.-Amen.

941
01:48:51.999 --> 01:48:53.999
Physician! 

942
01:48:53.999 --> 01:48:55.999
How is the Sultan doing? 

943
01:48:56.999 --> 01:48:58.999
He is still unconscious.

944
01:48:58.999 --> 01:48:59.999
Hmm...

945
01:48:59.999 --> 01:49:03.999
The arrows were poisoned. But by Allah's grace he's still breathing.

946
01:49:04.999 --> 01:49:09.999
 Prayer chants... 

947
01:49:22.999 --> 01:49:25.999
Uncle, I am here to inquire about your health.

948
01:49:41.999 --> 01:49:47.999
You killed my Uncle for the throne. And I killed you, Uncle! 

949
01:49:48.999 --> 01:49:51.999
Now Itaat Khan will be the new Sultan.

950
01:50:22.999 --> 01:50:29.999
To become the Sultan, you need strong ambition and a stronger will! 

951
01:50:39.999 --> 01:50:41.999
Praise be to Allah! 

952
01:50:41.999 --> 01:50:43.999
The Sultan is conscious again! 

953
01:50:44.999 --> 01:50:47.999
Praise be to Allah! 

954
01:50:48.999 --> 01:50:50.999
Long live the Sultan! 

955
01:50:50.999 --> 01:50:52.999
Long live! 

956
01:51:01.999 --> 01:51:03.417
Greetings, My Queen.

957
01:51:03.999 --> 01:51:04.999
The palanquins are ready to leave.

958
01:51:05.417 --> 01:51:06.999
By tonight we must...-Tomorrow morning.

959
01:51:08.999 --> 01:51:12.999
We will reach when the Khilji army is busy praying.

960
01:51:14.999 --> 01:51:16.999
It will be easier to get to the King.

961
01:51:16.999 --> 01:51:19.999
What are you doing, My Queen? 

962
01:51:19.999 --> 01:51:21.999
The map of Khilji's fort.

963
01:51:22.999 --> 01:51:27.417
When Rajputs don the saffron colour, they bathe their enemy in blood.

964
01:51:34.999 --> 01:51:35.999
Sultan! 

965
01:51:36.999 --> 01:51:38.999
Congratulations! 

966
01:51:38.999 --> 01:51:40.999
You fool! Mind the wounds.

967
01:51:40.999 --> 01:51:42.999
There's good news! 

968
01:51:42.999 --> 01:51:45.999
The palanquins from Chittor have reached our borders.

969
01:51:45.999 --> 01:51:49.999
Queen Padmavati will reach by tomorrow morning.

970
01:51:49.999 --> 01:51:51.999
Glory be to God! 

971
01:51:52.999 --> 01:51:53.999
Glory be to God! 

972
01:51:55.999 --> 01:51:58.999
She's arriving at a time when I am not in a condition to welcome her personally.

973
01:51:58.999 --> 01:52:04.999
Don't worry Sultan. I will personally escort her to you, with great fanfare! 

974
01:52:04.999 --> 01:52:09.999
I will welcome her in the Sultan's absence. Not you! 

975
01:52:10.999 --> 01:52:12.999
If the Sultan wishes so.

976
01:52:12.999 --> 01:52:14.999
Even I don't want any man to go near Queen Padmavati.

977
01:52:15.417 --> 01:52:16.999
Her decision is apt.

978
01:52:16.999 --> 01:52:18.999
As you wish, Sire! 

979
01:52:18.999 --> 01:52:23.999
The Empress of India will welcome the Queen of Chittor.

980
01:52:24.999 --> 01:52:25.999
Wonderful! 

981
01:52:30.999 --> 01:52:39.999
 Islamic call to Prayer... 

982
01:53:06.999 --> 01:53:12.000
Inform the Queen of Chittor that Mehrunisa, empress of India, is here to welcome her.

983
01:53:26.999 --> 01:53:28.999
You're truly a miracle of God! 

984
01:53:28.999 --> 01:53:31.999
Such beauty can even make angels have a change of heart.

985
01:53:31.999 --> 01:53:33.999
The Sultan is only human.

986
01:53:33.999 --> 01:53:34.999
And a culprit too.

987
01:53:36.999 --> 01:53:39.999
As per my conditions, I will first meet the King.

988
01:53:40.999 --> 01:53:45.999
And until he is set free, gora and Sujaan Singh will be by my side.

989
01:53:46.999 --> 01:53:47.999
Please come this way.

990
01:53:53.999 --> 01:53:56.999
All maids, step out of the palanquins.

991
01:54:59.999 --> 01:55:00.999
Malik...

992
01:55:00.999 --> 01:55:01.999
Yes, Sire? 

993
01:55:02.999 --> 01:55:05.999
Can you see any wound other than my bleeding heart? 

994
01:55:05.999 --> 01:55:06.999
No.

995
01:55:07.000 --> 01:55:11.999
Remember, no guard should be around, when the Queen arrives.

996
01:55:11.999 --> 01:55:16.999
Be rest assured, Sire. Your solitude will not be interrupted.

997
01:55:23.999 --> 01:55:33.999
 Islamic Prayer... 

998
01:55:34.999 --> 01:55:38.999
Greetings, Your Highness.

999
01:55:48.999 --> 01:55:50.999
My King! 

1000
01:55:55.999 --> 01:55:58.999
Has Mewar bowed down to the enemy? 

1001
01:55:59.999 --> 01:56:00.999
No.

1002
01:56:00.999 --> 01:56:02.999
Have you accepted the Sultan's conditions? 

1003
01:56:04.999 --> 01:56:04.999
No.

1004
01:56:05.000 --> 01:56:07.999
Then why are you here? 

1005
01:56:08.999 --> 01:56:10.999
I am here to set you free.

1006
01:56:10.999 --> 01:56:12.999
Mewar needs you.

1007
01:56:15.999 --> 01:56:17.999
Empress, now that I have arrived. Please release him.

1008
01:56:17.999 --> 01:56:19.999
Most certainly.

1009
01:56:19.999 --> 01:56:24.999
Hajuriya, please inform the Sultan that I will bring the Queen to him shortly.

1010
01:56:24.999 --> 01:56:26.999
Certainly.

1011
01:56:28.999 --> 01:56:31.999
Now listen to me carefully. We don't have much time.

1012
01:56:32.999 --> 01:56:34.999
I will take you both to the secret tunnel.

1013
01:56:34.999 --> 01:56:36.999
It will get you across our borders.

1014
01:56:37.999 --> 01:56:39.999
Why are you helping us? 

1015
01:56:40.999 --> 01:56:42.999
I am doing this for myself.

1016
01:56:43.999 --> 01:56:46.999
I am saving my Sultan from committing a heinous crime.

1017
01:56:54.999 --> 01:56:58.999
-The prayers will soon be over. We need to hurry! 

1018
01:56:58.999 --> 01:57:03.999
You need to leave before the guards are back.

1019
01:57:04.999 --> 01:57:05.999
Wait, My Queen.

1020
01:57:06.999 --> 01:57:08.999
I won't leave without meeting Alauddin.

1021
01:57:08.999 --> 01:57:11.999
That could be dangerous for you.

1022
01:57:11.999 --> 01:57:12.999
Your life could be in danger too.

1023
01:57:12.999 --> 01:57:14.999
Allah is my protector.

1024
01:57:14.999 --> 01:57:17.999
For God's sake you must forsake this thought.

1025
01:57:17.999 --> 01:57:23.999
Empress Mehrunisa, I am a Rajput. We never leave with our backs turned.

1026
01:58:00.999 --> 01:58:02.999
Oh! 

1027
01:58:03.999 --> 01:58:07.999
King Ratan Singh! How did you get to my court? 

1028
01:58:07.999 --> 01:58:12.999
I had warned you. You won't be able to stop the storm rising from Chittor.

1029
01:58:13.999 --> 01:58:20.999
I am so unfortunate. Each time I dream of meeting Queen Padmavati, you interrupt me.

1030
01:58:20.999 --> 01:58:26.999
And you're so unfortunate that I cannot show you my hospitality today.

1031
01:58:26.999 --> 01:58:29.999
You were never worthy of being a host.

1032
01:58:30.999 --> 01:58:32.999
Now you are not even worth being my enemy.

1033
01:58:33.999 --> 01:58:35.999
But you're still worthy, aren't you? 

1034
01:58:35.999 --> 01:58:37.999
Here...

1035
01:58:37.999 --> 01:58:40.999
Today is your opportunity. Pick up this sword and sever my head.

1036
01:58:40.999 --> 01:58:46.999
Because if you leave me alive today, you'll regret it forever.

1037
01:58:46.999 --> 01:58:49.999
You're lucky your enemy is a Rajput.

1038
01:58:53.999 --> 01:58:56.999
We don't attack the wounded and helpless.

1039
01:58:56.999 --> 01:59:02.999
You are so nice! And so are your ethics! 

1040
01:59:02.999 --> 01:59:04.999
You should learn some ethics too Alauddin.

1041
01:59:05.999 --> 01:59:07.999
They will make you into a human being.

1042
01:59:07.999 --> 01:59:11.999
My dear, there are no rules in love and war.

1043
01:59:12.417 --> 01:59:15.999
Without rules, your battle will be remembered as a blemish in history.

1044
01:59:15.999 --> 01:59:17.999
I will set that page in history on fire.

1045
01:59:17.999 --> 01:59:22.999
History isn't just written on paper which you can burn.

1046
01:59:23.999 --> 01:59:28.999
The day you're able to lift that sword we shall meet in the battlefield.

1047
01:59:31.999 --> 01:59:39.999
I am leaving with my pride, my Queen, from your fort and right in front of your eyes.

1048
01:59:41.999 --> 01:59:44.999
These wounds will take time to heal.

1049
01:59:45.999 --> 01:59:48.999
Until then my sword hangs over your head.

1050
01:59:58.999 --> 02:00:00.999
Ulugh Khan! 

1051
02:00:00.999 --> 02:00:03.999
Ulugh Khan! 

1052
02:00:04.999 --> 02:00:08.999
The Sultan has issued orders. Troops will be here any moment.

1053
02:00:09.999 --> 02:00:11.999
Please leave immediately through the tunnel.

1054
02:00:15.999 --> 02:00:16.999
Gora Singh, let's go.

1055
02:00:16.999 --> 02:00:17.999
You proceed, My Lord.

1056
02:00:18.999 --> 02:00:20.999
I'll stop the enemy's army from following you.

1057
02:00:21.999 --> 02:00:22.999
We shall meet at Chittor.

1058
02:00:23.999 --> 02:00:24.999
Hail Almighty! 

1059
02:00:26.999 --> 02:00:27.999
Hail Almighty! 

1060
02:00:31.999 --> 02:00:33.999
Dilawar! 

1061
02:00:33.999 --> 02:00:35.999
Dilawar! 

1062
02:00:35.999 --> 02:00:38.999
Dilawar!  Seal the gates! 

1063
02:00:38.999 --> 02:00:39.999
What happened Commander? 

1064
02:00:39.999 --> 02:00:42.999
We've been deceived. The enemy is within the fort.

1065
02:00:42.999 --> 02:00:45.999
Charge! 

1066
02:01:05.999 --> 02:01:06.999
Goodbye.

1067
02:01:17.999 --> 02:01:20.999
Charge! 

1068
02:01:29.999 --> 02:01:30.999
War Cry! 

1069
02:01:49.999 --> 02:01:51.999
Bad news, Sultan.

1070
02:01:51.999 --> 02:01:53.999
The Empress has foiled our plans.

1071
02:01:54.999 --> 02:01:56.999
Queen Padmavati and Ratan Singh have escaped.

1072
02:01:56.999 --> 02:02:02.999
Is love written in my destiny? 

1073
02:02:07.999 --> 02:02:11.999
Can you write it for me? 

1074
02:02:12.999 --> 02:02:13.999
No.

1075
02:02:58.999 --> 02:03:02.999
The glorious warriors who wielded their swords.

1076
02:03:03.999 --> 02:03:09.999
The brave-hearts who fought valiantly.

1077
02:03:12.999 --> 02:03:21.999
We salute the fearless Gora and Badal...

1078
02:03:21.999 --> 02:03:27.999
Who guarded the honour of Mewar.

1079
02:03:42.999 --> 02:03:44.999
Sultan.

1080
02:03:44.999 --> 02:03:46.999
Now what should we call her? 

1081
02:03:46.999 --> 02:03:49.999
Empress or a traitor? 

1082
02:04:14.999 --> 02:04:17.999
My own people have deceived me.

1083
02:04:19.999 --> 02:04:22.999
Itaat's arrows have injured me all over.

1084
02:04:22.999 --> 02:04:26.999
But your disloyalty broke my heart.

1085
02:04:27.999 --> 02:04:32.999
I loved you immensely but you betrayed me.

1086
02:04:32.999 --> 02:04:37.999
You took away my life's biggest dream.

1087
02:04:38.999 --> 02:04:41.999
Now I shall take away your identity...

1088
02:04:41.999 --> 02:04:46.999
...your imperial title, the joy out of your life.

1089
02:04:48.999 --> 02:04:54.999
Before I leave for Chittor, my last wish for you.

1090
02:04:55.999 --> 02:04:58.999
As I loved you immensely.

1091
02:05:01.999 --> 02:05:04.999
May you stay happy, prosperous...

1092
02:05:05.999 --> 02:05:06.999
... And blessed always.

1093
02:05:15.999 --> 02:05:16.999
Malik! 

1094
02:05:17.000 --> 02:05:18.999
Yes, Sire.

1095
02:05:19.999 --> 02:05:23.999
Before my rage buries her alive...

1096
02:05:24.999 --> 02:05:27.999
...take her to the dungeons.

1097
02:05:27.999 --> 02:05:29.999
As you say.

1098
02:05:30.999 --> 02:05:33.999
Before I leave, I'll make a wish for you too.

1099
02:05:34.999 --> 02:05:37.999
May all your dreams realise.

1100
02:05:39.999 --> 02:05:42.999
But your dream of getting Padmavati shall never come true.

1101
02:06:13.999 --> 02:06:16.999
-All hail Queen Padmavati! 

1102
02:06:16.999 --> 02:06:19.999
All hail King Ratan Singh! 

1103
02:06:36.999 --> 02:06:37.999
-My Queen...

1104
02:06:37.999 --> 02:06:41.999
The King and Queen Padmavati have entered the fort.

1105
02:06:41.999 --> 02:06:43.999
Everyone's making preparations to welcome them.

1106
02:06:44.000 --> 02:06:45.999
When everyone's busy welcoming them.

1107
02:06:46.999 --> 02:06:47.999
Then what should I do? 

1108
02:06:47.999 --> 02:06:49.999
Welcome them. What else? 

1109
02:06:50.999 --> 02:06:53.999
Queen Padmavati achieved what she set out for.

1110
02:06:53.999 --> 02:06:54.999
That is no ordinary feat.

1111
02:06:55.999 --> 02:06:58.999
So I'd suggest that you come along and welcome them too! 

1112
02:06:58.999 --> 02:07:00.999
You're not going anywhere, Kesar.

1113
02:07:01.999 --> 02:07:05.999
Go and get me a needle and thread.

1114
02:07:05.999 --> 02:07:09.834
I will. But first I must touch Queen Padmavati's feet.

1115
02:07:13.999 --> 02:07:15.999
My Lord, we have all heard the legend of Savitri.

1116
02:07:16.999 --> 02:07:20.999
Who fought the Lord of Death and brought her husband back to life.

1117
02:07:21.999 --> 02:07:25.999
Today I've started believing in that tale.

1118
02:07:38.999 --> 02:07:40.999
All hail Queen Padmavati! 

1119
02:07:40.999 --> 02:07:42.999
Welcome back, My Queen! 

1120
02:07:50.999 --> 02:07:53.999
Today you must not cheer for us...

1121
02:07:53.999 --> 02:07:57.999
But those martyrs, who laid down their lives for Mewar.

1122
02:07:58.999 --> 02:08:02.999
Those who sacrificed their lives to save ours.

1123
02:08:03.999 --> 02:08:05.999
As long as Chittor exists...

1124
02:08:05.999 --> 02:08:08.999
... Gora and Badal's names will be remembered.

1125
02:08:08.999 --> 02:08:12.999
All hail the late Commander, Gora Singh! 

1126
02:08:12.999 --> 02:08:16.999
All hail the brave Badal Singh! 

1127
02:08:19.999 --> 02:08:21.999
Congratulations, My Queen.

1128
02:08:21.999 --> 02:08:23.999
You brought our King back.

1129
02:08:24.999 --> 02:08:27.999
You can look in the mirror again.

1130
02:08:28.999 --> 02:08:31.999
Now everyone will worship you like a Goddess...

1131
02:08:31.999 --> 02:08:32.999
We couldn't save Badal! 

1132
02:08:35.999 --> 02:08:39.999
The Rajputs who lay down their lives in the battlefield never die.

1133
02:08:40.999 --> 02:08:41.999
They become immortal! 

1134
02:08:42.999 --> 02:08:46.999
It was my son's duty to fight for Mewar.

1135
02:08:46.999 --> 02:08:48.999
He attained martyrdom.

1136
02:08:50.999 --> 02:08:53.999
Shedding tears for him...

1137
02:08:55.999 --> 02:08:58.999
I finally realised why Rajputs are called brave-hearts...

1138
02:09:00.999 --> 02:09:02.999
... Because they have such brave mothers.

1139
02:09:05.999 --> 02:09:08.999
This evening has come after a long time.

1140
02:09:10.999 --> 02:09:13.999
You must look your best when you meet the King.

1141
02:09:31.999 --> 02:09:35.999
Khusrau, the river of love, runs in strange directions.

1142
02:09:35.999 --> 02:09:40.000
Whoever takes a plunge, drowns, and those who drown, find a shore.

1143
02:09:40.999 --> 02:09:41.999
Marvellous! 

1144
02:09:42.999 --> 02:09:45.999
You're fortunate that you can narrate your pain...

1145
02:09:45.999 --> 02:09:48.999
...while I feel suffocated.

1146
02:09:50.999 --> 02:09:52.999
I cannot bear this failure anymore.

1147
02:09:53.000 --> 02:09:55.999
Sultan, what can I do to ease your pain? 

1148
02:09:56.999 --> 02:09:59.999
As soon as we reach Chittor, write a message.

1149
02:09:59.999 --> 02:10:04.999
Maybe you can narrate my emotions with your poetic touch.

1150
02:10:04.999 --> 02:10:05.999
What do I write, Sultan? 

1151
02:10:06.999 --> 02:10:07.999
That...

1152
02:10:08.999 --> 02:10:11.999
I will only wait for one more night.

1153
02:10:11.999 --> 02:10:14.999
Fulfil the Sultan's wish, or else...

1154
02:10:14.999 --> 02:10:16.999
... Be ready to face his wrath.

1155
02:10:36.999 --> 02:10:38.999
-There you are! 

1156
02:10:38.999 --> 02:10:43.999
What I feared has come true. Alauddin has returned.

1157
02:10:43.999 --> 02:10:46.000
This time with an even bigger army! 

1158
02:10:55.999 --> 02:10:58.999
You rubbed salt on his wounds.

1159
02:10:59.999 --> 02:11:00.999
This was bound to happen.

1160
02:12:34.999 --> 02:12:37.999
Be patient Sultan. They will reply soon.

1161
02:12:38.999 --> 02:12:41.999
Give the Rajputs some time to think.

1162
02:12:41.999 --> 02:12:43.999
How much more time do they want? 

1163
02:12:43.999 --> 02:12:48.999
They'll have no option but to present Queen Padmavati to you by tomorrow morning.

1164
02:12:52.000 --> 02:12:55.999
I will wait from now on...

1165
02:12:57.999 --> 02:12:58.999
Under the scorching heat? 

1166
02:12:58.999 --> 02:13:03.999
I don't want to miss the moment when the doors of the fort open and she comes out.

1167
02:13:03.999 --> 02:13:06.999
I want to be the first one to see her.

1168
02:13:20.999 --> 02:13:29.999
 Sanskrit Prayer chants... 

1169
02:13:43.999 --> 02:13:47.999
Hail the Goddess! 

1170
02:14:03.999 --> 02:14:04.999
What happened? 

1171
02:14:05.999 --> 02:14:08.999
My sword looks stunning in your hands.

1172
02:14:08.999 --> 02:14:11.999
The sword is the most precious jewel of warriors.

1173
02:14:14.999 --> 02:14:16.999
It's our pride.

1174
02:14:17.999 --> 02:14:19.999
If it's our pride, then why are your eyes moist? 

1175
02:14:20.999 --> 02:14:22.999
Do you fear that I might not return from this war? 

1176
02:14:23.999 --> 02:14:26.999
Padmavati has never feared anything in her life.

1177
02:14:29.000 --> 02:14:31.999
Can I ask you for something tonight? 

1178
02:14:31.999 --> 02:14:35.999
There's nothing more you can ask for except for my heart.

1179
02:14:36.999 --> 02:14:37.999
I can.

1180
02:14:44.999 --> 02:14:46.999
The right of Jauhar. 

1181
02:14:49.999 --> 02:14:53.999
I cannot even die without your permission.

1182
02:15:29.999 --> 02:15:33.999
One heart.

1183
02:15:34.999 --> 02:15:39.999
One life.

1184
02:15:40.999 --> 02:15:54.999
I shall sacrifice for you.

1185
02:15:57.000 --> 02:16:01.999
There's me.

1186
02:16:01.999 --> 02:16:06.999
And my faith.

1187
02:16:06.999 --> 02:16:18.999
I shall sacrifice for you.

1188
02:16:19.999 --> 02:16:24.999
One heart.

1189
02:18:14.999 --> 02:18:15.999
Fire! 

1190
02:18:50.999 --> 02:18:53.999
What is this? I've never seen a weapon like this before! 

1191
02:19:24.999 --> 02:19:26.999
It's time for me to leave.

1192
02:19:29.999 --> 02:19:30.999
Hmm.

1193
02:20:10.999 --> 02:20:13.999
It's the right time to move our army forward, Sultan.

1194
02:20:13.999 --> 02:20:14.999
Not yet.

1195
02:20:16.000 --> 02:20:18.999
The walls of the fort are crumbling.

1196
02:20:19.999 --> 02:20:25.999
Soon they will have no choice but to face us in the battlefield.

1197
02:21:34.999 --> 02:21:39.000
My Lord, the army is waiting for your orders to attack.

1198
02:21:39.999 --> 02:21:40.999
No, Sujaan Singh.

1199
02:21:40.999 --> 02:21:42.000
I will go alone.

1200
02:21:42.999 --> 02:21:43.999
But My Lord...

1201
02:21:43.999 --> 02:21:46.999
This battle is between Alauddin and me.

1202
02:21:51.999 --> 02:21:54.999
Sire, why is he riding alone? 

1203
02:21:54.999 --> 02:21:56.999
To fight the Sultan, what else? 

1204
02:21:57.999 --> 02:21:58.999
Shall I go...? 

1205
02:21:58.999 --> 02:21:59.999
No.

1206
02:22:00.999 --> 02:22:02.999
Only a diamond can cut diamond.

1207
02:24:16.999 --> 02:24:21.999
In every age, a war for righteousness is fought between good and evil.

1208
02:24:22.999 --> 02:24:24.999
Like the one between Lord Ram and Raavan,

1209
02:24:25.999 --> 02:24:29.999
between the Pandavas and Kauravas and now between the Rajputs and Khiljis.

1210
02:24:30.999 --> 02:24:33.999
And each time, the good triumphs.

1211
02:24:34.999 --> 02:24:39.999
Today, thousands of Rajputs have set out to protect our dignity.

1212
02:24:40.999 --> 02:24:46.999
Chittor's walls have always shielded us. But today our soldiers stand guard.

1213
02:24:50.999 --> 02:24:52.999
For us, they are no less than God.

1214
02:24:54.999 --> 02:24:59.999
-When a Rajput fights for his motherland, the echo of his sword resonates through the ages.

1215
02:25:01.999 --> 02:25:04.999
-Whenever darkness engulfs the earth,

1216
02:25:04.999 --> 02:25:10.999
-Rajputs sacrifice their lives to spread light and uphold truth and freedom.

1217
02:25:30.999 --> 02:25:33.999
No, Malik Kafur. This is against the rules of warfare.

1218
02:25:33.999 --> 02:25:36.999
All is fair for the Sultan's victory.

1219
02:26:48.999 --> 02:26:52.000
You could've at least fought this battle with integrity.

1220
02:26:53.999 --> 02:26:55.999
There's only one rule in the battlefield...

1221
02:26:57.999 --> 02:26:59.000
Victory! 

1222
02:27:12.999 --> 02:27:13.999
Attack! 

1223
02:27:16.999 --> 02:27:18.999
Charge! 

1224
02:27:33.999 --> 02:27:39.999
-If our brave-hearts attain martyrdom today, the enemy would still not be victorious.

1225
02:27:40.999 --> 02:27:44.999
Chittor will witness another war, one that is unseen and unheard of.

1226
02:27:45.999 --> 02:27:46.999
And that war will be fought by us women! 

1227
02:27:49.999 --> 02:27:53.999
Our enemies shall watch how we turn our agony into victory.

1228
02:27:54.999 --> 02:28:00.999
It is time to reignite the holy fire that stood witness to our oath, that only death will do us apart.

1229
02:28:02.999 --> 02:28:08.999
We shall offer ourselves to the holy fire and perform Jauhar!  

1230
02:28:13.999 --> 02:28:18.999
Those who lust for our body, would not even get their hands on our shadows! 

1231
02:28:19.999 --> 02:28:24.999
Our bodies will be reduced to ashes, but our pride and honour will remain immortal.

1232
02:28:25.999 --> 02:28:29.999
And that will be the biggest defeat of Alauddin's life! 

1233
02:28:31.999 --> 02:28:32.999
My Queen...

1234
02:28:32.999 --> 02:28:34.999
Our King is no more! 

1235
02:28:45.999 --> 02:28:47.999
The time has come to don the veil of fire.

1236
02:28:51.999 --> 02:28:53.999
Shut the gates of the fort.

1237
02:28:55.999 --> 02:28:58.999
Shut the gates! 

1238
02:30:16.999 --> 02:30:19.999
Charge! 

1239
02:30:48.999 --> 02:30:51.999
Charge! 

1240
02:34:09.999 --> 02:34:15.999
Hail the Goddess! 

1241
02:37:56.999 --> 02:38:00.999
Queen Padmavati's Jauhar was the biggest defeat of Alauddin's life.

1242
02:38:01.999 --> 02:38:03.999
And Chittor's greatest victory.

1243
02:38:04.999 --> 02:38:11.999
Centuries later, the tale of her valour and sacrifice echoes in the heart of India.

1244
02:38:12.999 --> 02:38:19.999
To this day, she is worshipped as the Goddess Queen, the destroyer of evil.
